1
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:28,890
字幕翻译: Lvs
Translated By Lvs

2
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:33,890
发行网站: http://unity.starwcn.net
=====老鹰出品[Glede]======

3
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,500
Hello, 山下的伙计们
Hello, folks at home.

4
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:11,270
我离珠峰峰顶只有不到100码了
I'm 100 yards from the top of Mt. Everest.

5
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:14,900
但说实在的,这样的假期实在太闷了...
Yet there's a part of me
that can't wait to end this silly vacation...

6
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:18,410
...还不如回去工作来得刺激些
...and get back to work,
where the real challenges await.

7
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:22,100
先生,您不再考虑一下吗?
Shouldn't you take your age
into consideration, sir?

8
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,240
毕竟,您已经82岁了
After all, you're 82 years old.

9
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,920
我82岁?
Am I 82?

10
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:29,990
这些数字对我毫无意义,
我的冒险才开始
These numbers mean nothing to me.
My journey through life has just begun.

11
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,590
先生! 先生!
Sir! Sir!

12
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,860
- 暴风雪正在增强
- 情况非常危险
-Oota tells me the storm's getting worse.
-Very, very bad.

13
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:38,190
我们必须马上下山
We must abandon our ascent and
go down the mountain immediately.

14
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:41,290
可峰顶就在眼前,小子
We're so very close to the top,
Mr. Puffy Jacket Man.

15
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:45,300
我要下山了,你最也好下去
I'm heading down now, sir.
I advise you to do the same.

16
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:46,700
好吧,随便你
All right, so be it.

17
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:50,710
星期一开会再见,我会带上炸甜圈
See you at the staff meeting on Monday.
And I'll bring the Krispy Kremes!

18
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,690
这悲惨的画面今天一直出现在我们面前
There, once again, the sad footage
we've been watching all day.

19
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:17,770
Preston Blake，这位可敬的梦想家,
从拥有一家电台变成当今世界的传媒巨子
A beloved visionary who turned a single
radio station into a global media empire...

20
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:21,330
...离我们而去了,享年82岁.
稍后有详细报道
...Preston Blake, dead at 82. More after this.

21
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:27,940
您正收看的是Blake新闻网络
You're watching the Blake Broadcasting Network.

22
00:02:28,010 --> 00:02:30,740
Blake媒体公司--即本新闻网络的父公司,
The stock of Blake Media,
the parent company of this network...

23
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,410
...受Blake去世消息的影响,
其股票今早大幅下跌...
...plunged this morning
on the news of Blake's death...

24
00:02:33,490 --> 00:02:37,620
...在Blake的2号人物--Chuck Cedar
发表声明后,股价有所反弹
...but bounced back after a statement
by Blake's longtime number 2, Chuck Cedar.

25
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:39,990
就算华佗在世...
All the king's horses and all the king's men...

26
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:43,500
...Preston Blake也不能死而复生
...couldn't save Preston Blake
from becoming a human Popsicle.

27
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:48,430
据闻，Blake单身一人,
无儿无女，也未定下遗嘱
And sources indicate that Blake, who was
single and had no children, left no will.

28
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:52,600
那么，谁将会继承公司百分之49的股份...
So who inherits Blake's 49 percent stake
in the company's stock...

29
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:54,870
...也就是400亿美元呢?
...valued at $40 billion?

30
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:59,470
我们将与Blake先生周围的每个人接触
包括他的理发师...
We'll discuss that with people close
to Blake, including his longtime barber...

31
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:03,480
...敬请收看明天的"深入追击"
别错过, 我是Mac McGrath.
...on tomorrow's lnside Access.
Until then, I'm Mac McGrath.

32
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:07,450
- 拍好没有?
- 拍好了!
-Are we clear?
-Clear!

33
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:10,090
Babe? Babe在哪儿?
Babe? Where's Babe?

34
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,650
- 我不会放过你的!
- Babe!
-I'll come over and choke you to death.
-Babe!

35
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,060
我要挂电话了
I got to go.

36
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:16,620
不值一提的理发师!
你就这么点儿本事?
Freaking barber!
That's the best you could get me?

37
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,390
人们通常会和自己理发师聊很多事
People tell everything to their barbers.

38
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:22,930
他们是20多年的好朋友
He's been his closest confidant
for more than 20 years.

39
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,770
我不会让这家伙上节目,
你最好给我找点更好的东西，要快
I'm not putting this guy on the air.
Get me something better and get it quick.

40
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:28,470
不然你就有麻烦了
Or it's your ass.

41
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:34,640
继承人找到没有?
Did we find this heir yet?

42
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:37,750
马上就会有消息传真过来
We should be getting that information
via fax any minute now.

43
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:40,210
我正在叫人调查...
I have lawyers looking through birth records...

44
00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:43,080
...全国各地的出生记录,包括波多黎各和关岛
...in all 50 states, Puerto Rico and Guam.

45
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,650
我们还开了一个小小的赌局,
关岛的赔率是1000比1
In fact, we have a little pool going.
Guam's paying off at 1000-1.

46
00:03:48,330 --> 00:03:49,820
你觉得很好玩,是吧?
Is this a joke to you?

47
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:54,420
一个简单的血缘关系将会决定公司的命运
Some genetic lottery winner
now controls the fate of this company.

48
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:57,090
我不是这个意思,这的确很让人烦恼
No, I agree. It's troubling.

49
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:59,800
烦恼? 你满脸的胡子可以叫烦恼
Troubling? Your beard is troubling.

50
00:04:00,270 --> 00:04:04,470
你的破烟斗,还有你的一口黄牙都可以叫烦恼
Your pipe is troubling.
Your yellow teeth are really troubling.

51
00:04:04,710 --> 00:04:08,370
而如果我失去了公司,那就会是"灭顶之灾"
But if I lose control of this company,
it'll be catastrophic.

52
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:16,810
有谁认识 Mendlesohn医生?
Does anyone know a Dr. Mendlesohn?

53
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:20,090
恭喜你,你得了结肠痉挛
Congratulations, you have a spastic colon.

54
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,590
原来如此
That would explain a lot.

55
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,140
"Longfellow Deeds."
"Longfellow Deeds."

56
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:49,150
Chuck,我们应该到了
Chuck, I think we're there.

57
00:04:51,090 --> 00:04:52,790
老天啊,简直是一片野地
My God, it's all green.

58
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:02,260
瞧啊, 左侧有敌机!
Look at that thing. Fighter pilot on your left.

59
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,300
来啊,把它打下来!
Got that sucker!

60
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,550
你们俩迷路了么?
You guys lost?

61
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:24,420
我们在找Longfellow Deeds先生
We're looking for somebody: Longfellow Deeds.

62
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,020
那是Deeds的名字吗?
Is that Deeds' first name?

63
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:29,760
如果你指的是那位Longfellow Deeds先生...
If the Deeds you're referring to
is Longfellow Deeds...

64
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:32,090
...是的,那是他的名字
...then yes, that is Deeds' first name.

65
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,200
我可不知道Deeds的名字,我还以为是Greg呢
I don't know Deeds' first name. Maybe it's Greg.

66
00:05:35,530 --> 00:05:37,760
- 也许是Longfellow.
- 也许吧
-Maybe it's Longfellow.
-Maybe.

67
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:41,430
我不清楚,不过我知道有个家伙的名字叫Greg,
要不要我去叫他?
But I don't know. I know another guy
named Greg. You want me to call him?

68
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:44,600
不用了,谢谢
告诉我们Deeds先生住哪儿行么?
No! Thank you.
Please, just tell us where Deeds lives.

69
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:48,710
好吧,好吧,别着急!
我带你们去
All right, don't get all hyperactive.
I'll take you straight to him.

70
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:56,650
请进吧,伙计们
Step right in, fellows.

71
00:05:59,890 --> 00:06:02,880
- 他住批萨饼店?
- 谁会住在批萨饼店里呢！
-He lives at a pizzeria?
-You can't live in a pizzeria.

72
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,120
他住在楼上, 这店是他开的
He lives upstairs. He owns it.

73
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:07,500
劳驾请问，Deeds先生在么?
Excuse me. Is Mr. Deeds around?

74
00:06:07,570 --> 00:06:12,030
抱歉,他出去送货了,送货的家伙病了
No, I'm sorry, he's out making deliveries.
The regular delivery guy called in sick.

75
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:17,280
- 你看起来不象有病啊, Murph.
- 哎呀,我忘了自己在装病
-But you don't look too sick, Murph.
-I forgot I was faking sick today.

76
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:22,910
- 你们俩想把我骗回来,是吧
- Murph, 穿上围裙过来帮忙
-You two tricked me into coming here.
-Murph, put on an apron and give me a hand.

77
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:26,440
你们合起来耍我,对吧?
You guys played me like a fiddle. Touch?

78
00:06:27,490 --> 00:06:29,390
那么, Deeds太太在么?
Is Mrs. Deeds around?

79
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:32,420
Deeds 太太?
我看那小子连约会还没试过呢!
Mrs. Deeds?
I don't think that poor boy ever had a date.

80
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:36,660
- 那他什么时候回来?
- 一定在吃完午饭前,今天是"卡片日"
-Do you know when he'll be back?
-Before lunch is out. Today's Card Day.

81
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,990
- 卡片日?
- Deeds 经常会写一些贺卡
-Card Day?
-Deeds writes greeting cards.

82
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:42,230
每个星期一, 他会读给大家听,
然后挑一张...
Every Monday, he tries out a few
and then he chooses one...

83
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,830
...寄给贺卡公司
...and sends it to one of the big card companies.

84
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:47,240
虽然目前，他还没能卖出一张，但...
Now, he hasn't sold any yet, but...

85
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:48,730
...将来一定会的
...he will.

86
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,710
要来点什么?
You guys need anything else here?

87
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,650
"亲爱的：
"To my sweetheart

88
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,340
"我爱你，全心全意"
"I love you completely, with all my soul

89
00:06:57,550 --> 00:07:00,540
"我和你,就象面包奶油不分离"
"Without you I'm nothing, a butterless roll"

90
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,320
有意思
That's good.

91
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:04,650
喜欢吗,先生们?
Like that, gentlemen?

92
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,830
Hallmark贺卡公司觉得很不错,
很有发展潜力
Hallmark said it showed potential,
which is pretty cool.

93
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:11,190
- 你是Longfellow Deeds吗?
- 叫Deeds就行, 朋友
-Longfellow Deeds?
-Just call me Deeds, pal.

94
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:13,090
别叫Longfellow什么的那么麻烦
Easy with that Longfellow stuff.

95
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,070
我是Chuck Cedar, Blake媒体公司的执行总载
Chuck Cedar, CEO.

96
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:17,830
这位是Cecil Anderson, 法律主管
Cecil Anderson, General Counsel of Blake Media.

97
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:20,900
握手太见外了,我们流行拥抱
Handshakes are for strangers.
We hug around here, buddy.

98
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:23,200
你好吗, 欢迎来本镇
What's up? Welcome to town.

99
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:26,310
来吧,别不好意思
Come on, don't be shy.

100
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,520
胡子很漂亮,象林肯似的
请坐吧,兄弟们
I like that beard. Abe Lincoln-style.
Have a seat, boys.

101
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,840
- Murph!
- Deeds?
-Murph!
-Deeds?

102
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:34,950
- 你不是病了么?
- 我骗你的,朋友
-I thought you were sick today.
-That was a lie, pal.

103
00:07:35,050 --> 00:07:36,450
你玩我啊?
You fooled me.

104
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,680
- 是么?
- 是的
-I did?
-Yeah.

105
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,690
-  Deeds先生?
-  叫Deeds就行
-Mr. Deeds?
-Just Deeds.

106
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:43,720
听你电话里的声音好象病的很重,
好小子, 再说一遍听听
You sounded so sick on the phone.
You're good. Do that sick voice again.

107
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:47,920
Deeds, 我今天喉咙发炎没法上班了
Deeds, I can't come to work today.
I think I got strep throat.

108
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,630
难以置信,你完全可以去演广播剧什么的
That's unbelievable.
You could be a radio actor or something.

109
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:57,170
- 多谢,朋友
- Sure.
-Thanks, buddy.
-Sure.

110
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,280
Hey, Deeds. 快点读贺卡吧,
我还要回去值勤
Hey, Deeds. Read a card already.
I got to get back on duty.

111
00:08:01,910 --> 00:08:04,440
我得去了,很高兴见到两位
I'd better get up there.
Good meeting you, gentlemen.

112
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:07,420
Deeds先生, "Preston Blake"这个名字你熟悉吗?
Mr. Deeds, does the name Preston Blake
mean anything to you?

113
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:09,640
我妈界婚后姓 Blake
Mom's maiden name was Blake.

114
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:13,930
这星期只读一张,但我预感它会是一个转折点
Only one this week, but I got a feeling
it'll end my losing streak with Hallmark.

115
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:18,690
Preston Blake 是你母亲的叔叔
Preston Blake was your mother's uncle.

116
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:21,760
你不是开玩笑吧,我有个叔公?
真意外,他好么?
You're kidding me, I got an uncle?
Awesome. How's he doing?

117
00:08:21,830 --> 00:08:23,060
他死了
He's dead.

118
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:26,060
噢,真可惜,我有什么能帮忙的....
Oh, no. If there's anything I can do....

119
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:27,870
Deeds! Deeds!
Deeds! Deeds!

120
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:29,900
等等,伙计们
I'll be right with you guys.

121
00:08:31,610 --> 00:08:34,040
Blake死后留给你一大笔遗产
When Mr. Blake died,
he left an enormous fortune.

122
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:37,010
一共是...
$40 billion. He left it all...

123
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,050
...400亿美圆! 全是你的, Deeds.
...to you, Deeds.

124
00:08:41,350 --> 00:08:42,910
等会儿
Wait a minute.

125
00:08:44,090 --> 00:08:47,720
你刚才说什么? "我还要回去值勤"
你又不是警察!
What are you talking about, you got
to get back on duty? You're not a cop.

126
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:50,420
没错,警服是我买的
You're right.
I got this down at the costume shop.

127
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,260
扮扮警察有什么大不了的,哈哈!
But it can't hurt to pretend.

128
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:55,090
不知死活的家伙!
What a wisenheimer!

129
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,190
好吧,各位观众,表演开始
Okay, everybody, it's showtime.

130
00:08:59,070 --> 00:09:01,160
这是一张"结婚50周年卡"
I call this "50th Anniversary Card."

131
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:03,540
如今那可真的很难得
Which is quite a feat nowadays.

132
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:08,110
"50年风风雨雨"
"Fifty years have passed by
with laughter and tears

133
00:09:08,810 --> 00:09:11,040
"可曾记得,当年动物园中携手同游
"Do you remember when we went to the zoo

134
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,480
"把酒言欢"
"and that time we drank all the beers"

135
00:09:14,250 --> 00:09:15,240
干杯!
Beers!

136
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:20,290
"愿多陪你50载"
"I promise to love you for 50 years more

137
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:24,130
"哪怕老婆变肥婆"
"Even when your bosoms sag down to the floor"

138
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:28,430
太绝了! 他怎么想出来的?
That was awesome! How's he do it?

139
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,770
你以后不用再送批萨了, Deeds.
It looks like you won't have
to deliver pizza anymore, Deeds.

140
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,900
你现在富可敌国
You're a very rich man.

141
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,540
那和送批萨有什么关系?
What's that got to do with delivering pizzas?

142
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:42,280
女士们! 上面那盒是你们的
Ladies! The top one is yours.

143
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:44,370
-谢谢你, Deeds.
-当然
-Thank you, Deeds.
-Of course.

144
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:46,440
-真好吃!
-Deeds, 有什么新鲜事?
-Yummy!
-So, Deeds, what's new?

145
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:49,680
我刚知道自己有个叔公,不过他死了
I found out I have an uncle, but he died.

146
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:51,220
太遗憾了
That's too bad.

147
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:55,030
-但他留给我400亿美圆
-那是件好事
-He gave me $40 billion, though.
-Well, that's nice.

148
00:09:55,230 --> 00:09:56,130
Oh, 是啊!
Oh, yeah!

149
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:59,360
别把钱全花在那些录音机上
Don't you go and spend it all
on some fancy record player.

150
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,890
我不会的
I won't.

151
00:10:00,970 --> 00:10:02,560
这些是你朋友, Deeds?
Who are your friends, Deeds?

152
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:07,070
抱歉,Chuck, Cecil,
她们是Jane, Kitty and Sue.
I'm sorry.
Chuck, Cecil, this is Jane, Kitty and Sue.

153
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:11,440
-很高兴见到你, Cecil.
-是我的荣幸, Kitty(小猫)
-Pleasure to meet you, Cecil.
-Pleasure's all mine, Kitty.

154
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:14,440
还是叫你 "喵"
Or should I just say, "Meow"?

155
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:18,610
别发情了, Anderson.
Keep it in your pants, Anderson.

156
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:24,360
-这笔钱怎么会由我继承呢?
-你是Blake先生目前最近的亲戚了
-Now, why am I inheriting this money?
-You're Mr. Blake's closest living relative.

157
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,280
- 是吗? 没其他人了么?
- 没有,事实如此
-Really? He had nobody else?
-Nope, that's it.

158
00:10:27,590 --> 00:10:29,490
老天,我甚至没见过他!
Gosh, I never even met the guy.

159
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,490
帮我拿一下好么?
Would you hold this for a second?

160
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:38,000
Wetherley先生,你好吗?
Mr. Wetherley. How you doing, pal?

161
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:41,260
很好, Deeds. 正想去一趟药房
Very well, Deeds. Just going to the pharmacy.

162
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:43,670
好的,我帮你走快两步吧!
Well, let me get you there a little quicker.

163
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,040
- 你太太好么?
- 她很好
-How's your wife?
-She's fine.

164
00:10:49,110 --> 00:10:51,580
- 好极了,替我问候她
- 我会的
-Terrific. Say hi for me.
-I will.

165
00:10:51,650 --> 00:10:53,020
到了
Okay. Here you go.

166
00:10:54,350 --> 00:10:57,080
- 谢谢你背我, Deeds.
- 别客气
-Thanks for the lift, Deeds.
-You got it.

167
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:03,860
我们想请你去纽约,就几天时间
We need you to come back to New York with us.
Just for a few days.

168
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,400
要请你签几份文件
We're drawing up some papers
you'll need to sign.

169
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:07,690
什么文件?
What kind of papers?

170
00:11:08,070 --> 00:11:12,560
实际上,你已经继承了Blake媒体公司的
300万股份
Technically, you've inherited
300 million shares of Blake Media, lnc.

171
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:16,070
Chuck和我, 还有其他股东, 将会用...
Chuck and I, along with
some of the partners, will buy that stock...

172
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:19,410
...400亿美圆购买你的股份,
为此我们必须到处贷款--
...for $40 billion,
which we've had to borrow from various--

173
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,640
别提那些金融方面的麻烦事了!
Who cares about the financial mumbo jumbo?

174
00:11:21,710 --> 00:11:24,510
我们需要一些时间来玩文字游戏罢了
We need a little time
to dot the t's and cross the i's.

175
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:28,020
这段时间,我们希望你能够避开新闻界
And while we're doing that,
we need you to stay away from the press.

176
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:31,320
几星期后,此事会慢慢被遗忘....
The media frenzy will die down
in a couple weeks but until then....

177
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:35,190
你也不想这个小镇被记者们糟蹋,对吧?
You don't want reporters crawling
all over this lovely little town, do you?

178
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:36,620
Oh, 当然不!
Oh, no!

179
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:41,930
- 鬼眼!
- 什么?
-Crazy Eyes!
-What?

180
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:48,030
你好吗,朋友?
你要的批萨,是你最喜欢的口味
How you doing, pal?
I got your pizza, just the way you like it.

181
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,530
Oh, 太好了!
Oh, yes!

182
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,770
法国风味外加巧克力夹心饼, Deeds.
French fries and Oreos.
You know me all too well, Deeds.

183
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,410
你犯了什么事儿?
What are you in for?

184
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,950
因为袭击邮差,监禁一晚
I'm doing a one-nighter
for biting Ed the mailman.

185
00:11:58,250 --> 00:12:01,690
那家伙想给我下咒, 就象巫师之类
The guy was trying to cast a spell on me,
like a wizard.

186
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:06,660
- 你肯定?
- 不,或许他只是在招手?
-Are you sure about that?
-I don't know. Maybe he was just waving.

187
00:12:08,190 --> 00:12:11,750
- 他们是谁?
- 这是纽约来的Chuck 和Cecil
-Who are your friends?
-This is Chuck and Cecil from New York.

188
00:12:13,230 --> 00:12:14,460
我不喜欢他们
I don't like them.

189
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:16,800
好吧,很高兴见到你
Okay. Nice seeing you.

190
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:21,770
我从没去过纽约,可以去看看风景
I've never been to New York before.
I suppose I could check out the sights.

191
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:24,210
- 给我一小时准备一下,好么?
- 没问题
-Give me an hour to pack, okay?
-You got it.

192
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:28,240
我可能是自从Jimmy McNally去过迪斯尼后,
第一个离开本镇的人
I'll be the first guy to leave here since
Jimmy McNally went to Disney World.

193
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,240
过几天再见, 各位!
See you later, everybody!

194
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:39,280
明天是儿童免费日,别忘了把凳子弄干净
Tomorrow is "Kids Eat For Free" Day.
Don't forget to clean the highchairs.

195
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:41,760
别担心,我会打理好一切的
Don't worry, I'll take care of everything.

196
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:44,020
- 去吧,玩个痛快!
- 我会想你的
-Go, have a good time!
-I'll miss you.

197
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,190
再见,Jan. 再见, Murph.
'Bye, Jan. Smell you later, Murph.

198
00:12:48,030 --> 00:12:49,430
- 来张卡片吧!
- 对!
-Give us a card!
-Yeah!

199
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:56,100
"当我踏上旅途进城去"
"On my way to the big city for a business trip

200
00:12:56,610 --> 00:13:00,810
"从未离开过故乡,一个乡巴佬?
"Never, ever left Mandrake Falls before
Ain't that a pip

201
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:07,310
"当我离去,会惦记大家"
"But while I'm gone, I know I'll miss you all a lot"

202
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:11,690
"衣锦还乡时别忘了带上礼物"
"So bring your rich butt back here
and buy us all a shot"

203
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,050
没问题, pal!
You got it, pal!

204
00:13:19,570 --> 00:13:20,960
别乱跑
Take it easy.

205
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:33,530
发生了本年度最轰动的事件,
但我们竟然一无所获?
The biggest story of the year
and we've got nothing?

206
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:37,670
你们想去当个小报记者吗? 我不这么看!
Do you people want to be tabloid journalists?
Because I don't think so.

207
00:13:38,050 --> 00:13:40,920
为了新闻,你们必须不择手段
想当初...
You've got to be ruthless. When I started out...

208
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:43,890
...我躲在雪糕箱子里
...I slept in Tom and Roseanne's dumpster
for two days...

209
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,790
- ...在Tom和Roseanne的垃圾箱里足足呆了两天
- 有消息了!
-...disguised as a giant carton of ice cream.
-I got it!

210
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:49,980
我在Blake公司的消息人士说
公司的直升机...
My source at Blake says
the company helicopter...

211
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:53,520
... 今天中午起程飞往Mandrake山谷
...took off from there this afternoon
with two male passengers aboard...

212
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,570
-...有两名乘客
- 去哪儿?
-...headed for Mandrake Falls.
-Where?

213
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:57,930
新汉普郡的一个乡下小镇
Some little hick-ass town in New Hampshire.

214
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,770
但回来时有三名乘客
But now they're on their way back
with three male passengers.

215
00:14:02,470 --> 00:14:04,470
- 多了一个人!
- 聪明!
-That's one more!
-Duh!

216
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,450
干的好, Marty，第三个乘客就是我们要找的人
That third guy's our heir. Nice work, Marty.

217
00:14:08,510 --> 00:14:10,950
他们本应5点钟到达
They were supposed to arrive
at Blake Media at 5:00.

218
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,250
但他们在康涅狄格临时停留了一阵
But they made an unscheduled stop
in Connecticut.

219
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:16,050
能吃到这么好的东西真是太棒了！
I'm so happy I got the Big Bacon Classic.

220
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,590
谢谢你们，实在是太美味了
Thanks for stopping. This is unbelievable.

221
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:21,790
- 乐意效劳
- 觉得味道怎么样, Cecil?
-Happy to do it.
-How's that Frosty treating you, Cecil?

222
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:25,630
你胡子上沾了点东西，哈哈，骗你的
You got some on your beard. I'm just kidding.

223
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,430
瞧他多有意思！
I got him big time, man.

224
00:14:28,370 --> 00:14:30,600
两小时内节目就要开始
I'm going on the air in two hours' time.

225
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:34,700
到那时，我要知道他的一切
听见了吗, Jim.
And I want that guy's life story by then.
I'm talking to you, Jim.

226
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:37,570
还有, Babe. Babe?
And I'm also talking to you, Babe. Babe?

227
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:39,980
Babe死到哪儿去了?
Where the hell's Babe?

228
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:43,110
你又没去开会，Mac发火了
You missed another staff meeting. Mac's pissed.

229
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:46,580
等我把Blake的消息给他，他就会消气的
He won't be pissed when I crack this Blake story.

230
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:49,850
- 你有什么消息?
- 没有，你呢?
-What do you got?
-Nothing. Do you have anything?

231
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:52,180
我很快就会有大把消息了
I'll have a lot more in a few hours.

232
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,690
你得帮帮我
You got to be a pal.

233
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:57,350
我需要这个新闻，
我身无分文，而Mac还要炒了我
I need this story.
I'm flat broke and Mac is going to fire me.

234
00:14:57,430 --> 00:15:00,360
你会身无分文?
这儿就数你赚的最多了！
How're you flat broke?
You make more money than anyone here.

235
00:15:00,430 --> 00:15:02,300
- 你的钱都花哪儿去了?
- 买鞋
-What did you blow it on?
-Shoes.

236
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:05,290
明天中午我会把消息全告诉你
I'll tell you everything I know
over lunch tomorrow...

237
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:07,400
...这次别让你那个开CLUB的男朋友...
...as long as your club promoter boyfriend...

238
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:10,200
...再用摩托车撞我了
...doesn't try to run me over
with his motorcycle again.

239
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:14,140
别担心，我们最近没怎么来往
You're safe there.
Ken and I are kind of taking a break.

240
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:15,840
是吗? 你们分手了?
Really? So he moved out?

241
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:20,480
Babe, 干嘛睡在这儿? 我那儿有空房间
Babe, what are you staying here for?
I have a spare bedroom.

242
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:22,710
我去过你那儿,记得吗?
We tried that once, remember?

243
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:26,950
我睡醒时发现, 你喘着粗气站我床边
I woke up and you were standing
over my bed, breathing heavily.

244
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:30,120
我那是哮喘发作,找不到药
I was having an asthma attack.
I couldn't find my puffer.

245
00:15:33,130 --> 00:15:37,530
嘿,慢点, 伙计们
你们在打饱嗝啊!
Easy, fellows.
The Biggie Fries are making a comeback.

246
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:42,300
喜欢足球么? 帕特队今年可能夺得联合会杯
You guys football fans? The Pats
could take the conference this year.

247
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:45,400
海豚队没那么强,至于喷气机队只配掂底
The Dolphins are overrated
and the Jets are choke artists.

248
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,170
如果我是你,我可不会这么说, Deeds先生
I wouldn't say that, Mr. Deeds.

249
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:50,610
- 叫我Deeds就行. 你说为什么?
- 你是喷气机队的老板, Deeds.
-Just Deeds. Why is that, though?
-You own the Jets, Deeds.

250
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,010
是吗?
I do?

251
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:55,410
那可真没面子
That sucks.

252
00:15:56,490 --> 00:16:00,750
希望他们可别在总决赛碰上帕特队,
要不然,我宁愿去死好过些
I hope they don't play the Pats in the playoffs
or I'll have to kill myself.

253
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:04,930
我还是觉得有点担心
I'm still very worried about this.

254
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:09,260
你不是刚抽完大麻吧?
你担心什么呢!
What do you got in that pipe, hashish?
You're paranoid.

255
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:12,730
- 这小子简直是上天的恩赐
- 要是他不肯卖股份怎么办?
-This guy's perfect for us.
-What if he won't sell us his shares?

256
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,170
我既然能说服整个公司...
If I got Blake to trust me with his company...

257
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,870
...自然也能摆平这小子!
你看他!
...I can get this moron to do the same.
Look at him.

258
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,270
不错, Anderson.
That's right, Anderson.

259
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:01,220
够了!
Enough!

260
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:03,850
真扫兴
Party pooper.

261
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,890
老天爷!
Holy cow!

262
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,950
你好吗, 纽约?
What's up, New York?

263
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:16,590
我来啦!世界上最棒的城市!
It's an honor to come
to the greatest city in the world!

264
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:28,940
恭喜你, Deeds, 你现在是全纽约最
有钱的单身汉了!
Congratulations, Deeds, you're now
the most eligible bachelor in New York.

265
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:32,010
我可不想别人因为我有钱而追求我
I don't want to meet a girl
just because I'm wicked rich.

266
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,750
话虽如此, 但你去我们的俱乐部看看之后
That's nice, but let's see
how you stick to your guns...

267
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:38,150
或许就不会这么想了
...once you've paid a visit to one
of our many fine gentlemen's clubs.

268
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:38,980
是吗?
What?

269
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:41,660
我爸救过我妈的命
My father saved my mother.

270
00:17:41,730 --> 00:17:44,290
她当时滑冰掉进冰窟窿里
She was figure skating and fell through the ice.

271
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:48,090
我常想,我可能也得这样,够刺激的
I always thought I'd meet
a girl the same way. Bullspit like that.

272
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:52,000
看来,我要经常帮你留意
那些遇到麻烦的女士才行
Then I'll just keep a lookout
for ladies in distress, as it were.

273
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:54,130
- 那太好了
- 喂! Mandrake山谷来的 !
-That'd be nice.
-Hey, Mandrake Falls!

274
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,110
保安,抓住他!
Security, stop that guy!

275
00:17:58,510 --> 00:17:59,500
站住! 别跑!
Stop! Come back!

276
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:02,780
那张照片能值十万块,
而且不用一小时就会满天飞了
He'll get $100,000 for the picture.
It'll be on the news in an hour.

277
00:18:02,850 --> 00:18:05,750
他这套惊险动作也值这个价钱了
He deserves it with those
James Bond moves he just pulled.

278
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:09,580
不,他该被割断喉咙,无耻的家伙,
来吧,咱们走
No, he deserves to get his throat cut,
the filthy spy. Come on, let's go.

279
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,330
这就是我叔公的家?
So this is where my uncle lived?

280
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:22,960
是的, 他在这儿住了35年
Yes, sir. For the last 35 years
of his astonishing life.

281
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:26,670
- 你像是突然冒出来似的
- 我非常非常的敏捷, 先生
-You kind of snuck up on me there.
-I am very, very sneaky, sir.

282
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:29,510
我见识过了，我叫Deeds.
I see that. My name is Deeds.

283
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:32,080
我是Emilio, 先生，我是您的仆人
I am Emilio, sir. I am your servant.

284
00:18:32,410 --> 00:18:36,540
仆人？ 我可用不着什么仆人,
交个朋友倒是可以
Servant? I don't want a servant,
but if you want to be my friend, I'll take that.

285
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:38,710
朋友?
Friends.

286
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:41,150
没错,好朋友
Yes, good friends.

287
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:46,480
您想回房间去吗? 今天一定很劳累了吧
Would you like to go down to your apartment?
I'm sure it's been an exhausting day.

288
00:18:46,990 --> 00:18:49,520
- 你的意思呢, Chuck?
- 那里很安全
-That okay with you, Chuck?
-You'll be safe there.

289
00:18:49,590 --> 00:18:52,720
我们可能要花几天时间
来准备文件让你签字
It'll take us a couple days
to draw up the papers for you to sign.

290
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:54,790
- 在自己家里慢慢享受吧
- 妙极了
-Go make yourself at home.
-Terrific.

291
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,200
- 回头见
- 先生,我们一会儿见
-Later.
-I will be with you shortly, sir.

292
00:18:57,270 --> 00:19:00,330
好的,幸会了,我是Deeds
You got it. Nice to meet you. I'm Deeds.

293
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:03,870
- 我是Reuben, 先生
- 这电梯真是不错
-I'm Reuben, sir.
-This is a wicked nice elevator.

294
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:07,140
看好他, Emilio. 否则有你好瞧的
Keep an eye on him, Emilio. Or it's your ass.

295
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,840
见到您我很高兴,先生
It's nice to see you too, sir.

296
00:19:09,150 --> 00:19:11,710
这份工作怎么样, Reuben?
So how's the elevator business
treating you, Reuben?

297
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,750
"有起有落"!
It has its ups and downs.

298
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:16,280
没错! 没错!
All right! All right!

299
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,480
说的好!
That was good.

300
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:21,890
好家伙, 你怎么这么快啊?
Jeesum crow, how'd you get down here so fast?

301
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:24,820
身手敏捷, 先生, 这边走
Sneaky-sneaky, sir. Right this way.

302
00:19:28,630 --> 00:19:29,620
Wow.
Wow.

303
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:34,240
Wow.
Wow.

304
00:19:35,970 --> 00:19:37,670
怎么了,先生?
Is something the matter, sir?

305
00:19:40,410 --> 00:19:42,850
- 是回声,先生
- 是啊,你试试
-That's an echo, sir.
-Yeah, you try it.

306
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,410
- 我,先生?
- 很有意思的
-Me, sir?
-It's a lot of fun.

307
00:19:50,420 --> 00:19:52,480
来吧,大声点儿
Come on, you can do it louder than that.

308
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,800
- 厉害
- 谢谢你,先生
-Serious.
-Thank you, sir.

309
00:20:03,030 --> 00:20:05,730
嘿,朋友,想不想试试?
Hey, buddy, how you doing?
You want to give it a shot?

310
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:09,200
不错
Nice.

311
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:14,040
大家都想试试吗 ? 一起怪叫
You guys want to join us? Make a weird noise.

312
00:20:23,150 --> 00:20:26,920
真有意思, 不过我有点累了,想去睡觉
That was a great time. Well, I'm tired.
I'd like to go to sleep.

313
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:29,860
- 这边
- 谢谢你们, 大家去睡个好觉
-This way.
-Thank you very much. Good night, everyone.

314
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:31,290
晚安
Good night.

315
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:42,860
你是不是打算睡在那儿,直到邮报把新闻全抢走?
You just going to lie there
and let the Post take your story?

316
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,620
你好吗, 纽约?
What's up, New York?

317
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:12,530
屋里竟然有个饮水器,不错!
He had a water fountain in his room. I love it.

318
00:21:21,010 --> 00:21:22,670
是夏威夷果汁
That's Hawaiian Punch.

319
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:24,710
他喜欢...
He adored...

320
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,150
...夏威夷果汁
...Hawaiian Punch.

321
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:30,450
Wow! 又被你吓了一跳!
Wow! You kind of just snuck up on me there.

322
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:34,290
恐怕您还没适应我的敏捷
I fear you're underestimating the sneakiness, sir.

323
00:21:34,490 --> 00:21:37,190
可能吧,你在那儿干什么?
I guess I was. What are you doing down there?

324
00:21:37,460 --> 00:21:39,990
我帮您换袜子
I am assisting you with your sock change.

325
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:43,360
帮我换袜子? 不必了,起来吧
You'd change my socks for me?
You don't got to do that. Stand up.

326
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,230
谢谢您
Thank you.

327
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:46,900
而且,你一定不会想碰我的右脚
Besides, you don't want
to have to touch my right foot.

328
00:21:46,970 --> 00:21:50,670
我当童子军时,右脚严重冻伤,
你瞧
I got wicked bad frostbite when I was
in the Scouts. Check it out.

329
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,580
够恐怖的,是吧?
Pretty messed up, huh?

330
00:21:57,880 --> 00:22:02,110
一想起它,恐怕我这一辈子都会作恶梦
The hideousness of that foot
will haunt my dreams forever.

331
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,580
是的,有人也这么说过
Yeah, I've heard that before.

332
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:07,790
真正恐怖的是, 这只脚一点感觉都没有!
But the weird thing is I got no feeling left in it.

333
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:10,660
你就算用力踩,我也不会疼
So you could jump on it and it wouldn't hurt me.

334
00:22:10,930 --> 00:22:14,090
- 来,试试踩两脚
- 还是不必了吧,先生
-Go ahead, jump on it.
-I'd really rather not, sir.

335
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:15,690
踩吧, 求你了
Please jump on my foot.

336
00:22:26,310 --> 00:22:27,640
没感觉
I didn't feel that.

337
00:22:27,710 --> 00:22:31,810
你就这么大劲儿? 不如去壁炉那儿
把烧火棍拿来, 给我来几下结实的
What else you got? Get that
fireplace poker and whack my foot.

338
00:22:32,150 --> 00:22:35,780
- 一定要这么做吗?
- 多有意思啊,去拿吧
-Do I absolutely have to?
-It's going to be fun. Just grab it.

339
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:40,320
我的朋友有空时都喜欢这么干
All my friends do this when they're wasted.

340
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,730
来吧
Come on.

341
00:22:42,990 --> 00:22:44,460
来呀, 狠狠来几下
Go ahead, give it a whack.

342
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:49,460
- 没事儿
- 真的?
-Nothing.
-Really?

343
00:22:49,530 --> 00:22:50,800
恐怖吧?
Isn't that sick?

344
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,870
完全没感觉, 真变态, 接着打
Didn't feel that. Isn't that awesome? Go ahead.

345
00:22:54,940 --> 00:22:55,910
没事儿
Nothing.

346
00:22:56,670 --> 00:23:00,130
开始觉得过瘾了,对吧?
来呀! 别手下留情!
You're starting to like it, aren't you?
Chop that wood!

347
00:23:00,510 --> 00:23:01,810
没错,就是这样!
That's it!

348
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:06,920
啊！你这个变态的家伙！
你真狠啊!
You're sick! You're sick!
Why would you do that?

349
00:23:06,990 --> 00:23:08,920
我骗你的,朋友
I'm just kidding you, pal.

350
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:13,920
- 真被你吓着了
- 我看见了,你的样子....
-You had me going there.
-I saw your face, you were like....

351
00:23:15,630 --> 00:23:19,360
我要去问问Cedar和Anderson
今天该干什么呢?
I got to find out from Cedar and Anderson
what I'm supposed to do today.

352
00:23:19,430 --> 00:23:22,590
帮我把它拔出来好么, 我给钉在地上了
So could you take that out of my foot?
I'm nailed to the ground.

353
00:23:23,570 --> 00:23:24,590
行了
There you go.

354
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:28,400
我必须强调, 这次的会谈请各位保守秘密...
I must insist on absolute secrecy
regarding this discussion...

355
00:23:28,470 --> 00:23:31,070
...直到我正式获得Blake先生的全部股份
...till I've officially acquired Mr. Blake's shares.

356
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:33,630
如果那些内容可以接受的话,
在我看来...
If that's acceptable,
then as far as I'm concerned...

357
00:23:33,710 --> 00:23:36,200
...2000个电台已经是诸位的了
...you've just bought 2,000 radio stations.

358
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:38,780
早上好
Good morning.

359
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:41,170
Deeds.
Deeds.

360
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:42,750
大家在忙什么?
What's up?

361
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:44,690
一点生意上的事
Doing a little business.

362
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:51,330
这间房子也有回音, 你们一定知道
This room's an echo room, too.
I'm sure you guys already knew that.

363
00:23:52,730 --> 00:23:53,790
你有何贵干?
May I help you?

364
00:23:53,870 --> 00:23:56,960
只是来看看今天有什么事可干
I just wanted to see
if there's anything I should do today.

365
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:00,430
所有的事情都有人负责
I think we've got everything under control.

366
00:24:00,510 --> 00:24:05,140
总有点什么事吧? 在没签文件之前
这里还是属于我的,对吧?
There's got to be something. Until I sign
those papers I own this place, right?

367
00:24:06,710 --> 00:24:07,870
什么?
What?

368
00:24:08,350 --> 00:24:10,780
请各位稍等片刻
Ladies and gentlemen,
pardon me a moment, please.

369
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:11,780
当然
Of course.

370
00:24:12,050 --> 00:24:15,750
你好吗, 老兄? 我昨晚一直梦见冰天雪地, 你呢?
What's up, buddy? I was dreaming
about Frosties all last night. You?

371
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:18,480
我也一直在做梦,可是和你的不一样
I tried to make my own at home,
but it wasn't the same.

372
00:24:20,230 --> 00:24:21,210
Deeds.
Deeds.

373
00:24:21,290 --> 00:24:25,130
公司每个股东,无论大小,都有发言权
Every stockholder, large and small,
has a say in the operation of this company.

374
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:27,760
但那是在每年的股东大会上
They have this say
at the annual stockholders' meeting.

375
00:24:27,830 --> 00:24:31,460
其他的时间, 公司的运作是由行政人员
The other 364 days of the year,
the officers of the company, like me...

376
00:24:31,540 --> 00:24:34,330
- 比如我,来负责管理的
- 你的意思是我不应该插手
-...run the show.
-You mean now that my uncle's gone.

377
00:24:34,410 --> 00:24:36,740
是的,而且这也不是什么有意思的事
Yeah, and it's not all fun and games.

378
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:40,310
公司有太多的事情要处理...
This company is a player on so many levels
and in so many areas...

379
00:24:40,380 --> 00:24:43,640
...完全是24个小时工作制
...that running it is literally a 24-hour-a-day job.

380
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:46,880
我昨晚只睡了三个小时
I only got three hours of sleep last night.

381
00:24:47,250 --> 00:24:49,910
那应该是"21个小时工作制",对吧?
Then it's actually a 21-hour-a-day job, huh?

382
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:53,160
让开,小姐,
我才不管他妈的什么会议!
Move it, lady.
I don't give a damn about no meeting.

383
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:54,810
Cedar先生, 对不起--
Mr. Cedar, I am sorry--

384
00:24:55,260 --> 00:24:59,630
上个赛季我打了3500码, 现在我不干了
I passed for 3,500 yards last season
and I ain't gonna touch a football...

385
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:04,160
除非你们这帮有钱的混蛋
同意新的和约
...until you get off your fat, rich asses
and renegotiate my bullshit contract.

386
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:07,970
伙计,当着女士的面,说话要小心些
Easy with the language, buddy.
There are ladies present.

387
00:25:09,210 --> 00:25:11,570
你闭上嘴,有钱的臭小子!
Shut the hell up, rich boy!

388
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:15,770
马上给我加工资,否则你们这帮混--
I want more money, or you all can just suck my--

389
00:25:20,290 --> 00:25:21,410
我警告过你的
I warned you.

390
00:25:22,920 --> 00:25:26,720
说真的,你倒下去的样子活象一袋番茄,
来吧
You went down like a sack of potatoes,
I'll tell you that much. Come on.

391
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,760
起来吧,大块头
Come on, big man. Upsy-daisy.

392
00:25:30,930 --> 00:25:33,330
女士们先生们,足球!
Mesdames and Gentlemen, football!

393
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:36,690
你的合同是怎么回事?
What's the problem with your contract?

394
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:41,660
我认为如果我打的好,就应该签新的和约,
赚更多的钱!
I figured if I played well,
I'd renegotiate and get more money.

395
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:45,240
如果你打的不好,
我们能不能重新签约减少你的酬金呢?
If you didn't play well,
could we renegotiate and pay you less?

396
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:46,500
妈的, 休想!
Shit, no!

397
00:25:47,010 --> 00:25:48,670
我是说, 不行
I mean, no.

398
00:25:49,710 --> 00:25:51,840
这对我可不公平
Doesn't seem fair to me.

399
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:55,910
- 他是我们的得分手
- 我明白, Chuck. 让我处理吧
-He led the League in touchdown passes.
-That's okay, Chuck. I got this one.

400
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:59,180
听着,朋友们,我要提高工资...
Listen, fellows, I want more money...

401
00:25:59,590 --> 00:26:01,850
...否则我一场都不打了
...or I ain't even gonna play another down.

402
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:07,090
好吧, 我们只能请你走人了!
Well, we'll have to let you go then.

403
00:26:08,130 --> 00:26:10,970
-"请我走人"?
- 没错,你被解雇了
-"Let me go"?
-Yeah, you're fired.

404
00:26:12,600 --> 00:26:14,330
那么我可以与其他球队签约了?
So can I sign with another team?

405
00:26:14,410 --> 00:26:17,310
随便你,不过我建议你改变一下态度...
You can do anything.
I suggest you change your attitude...

406
00:26:17,380 --> 00:26:19,500
...否则,没人会愿意和你共事的
...or nobody will want to work with you.

407
00:26:21,050 --> 00:26:22,030
再见
'Bye.

408
00:26:23,610 --> 00:26:24,600
Deeds.
Deeds.

409
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:28,410
Kevin 两年前得了Heisman奖,
他是我们的顶尖球员
Kevin won the Heisman Trophy two years ago.
He is our best player.

410
00:26:28,490 --> 00:26:32,180
- 别担心,他会回来的
- 你们会后悔的!
-Don't worry, he'll be back.
-Biggest mistake of your lives!

411
00:26:32,490 --> 00:26:33,750
这东西真不错
This thing is cool.

412
00:26:34,490 --> 00:26:38,720
干嘛不出去走走, 去看看纽约,
好东西还多着呢, 带上这个
Why don't you get out and enjoy the city?
Everything's fine here. Take that with you.

413
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:42,250
还是留在这儿吧, 好吧, 有事尽管叫我
I'll leave it here. That's all right.
But call me if you need me.

414
00:26:42,330 --> 00:26:45,430
- 当然
- 谢谢, 再见 Anderson.
-Absolutely.
-Thanks. Love you, Anderson.

415
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:49,870
另外, 各位好像是法国人,
[法语]大家好!
All you guys, I noticed you were French.
The opposite of bonjour to you.

416
00:26:53,140 --> 00:26:54,740
你染金发可真性感
You look so hot as a blond.

417
00:26:54,810 --> 00:26:57,750
样子变化不大么？希望没人认得出我
It's not too streaky?
I feel like he did it really streaky.

418
00:26:57,820 --> 00:27:01,050
我喜欢你这个样子，不过还是让我去吧，
可能有危险的
I love it, but let me go undercover.
This could get dangerous.

419
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:05,220
他喜欢的是落难女子，不是浑身香水味的男人
He said he likes ladies in distress,
not men who wear too much cologne.

420
00:27:05,460 --> 00:27:07,720
- 他来了
- 谢谢你带我出来
-There he is.
-Thanks for the tour.

421
00:27:07,790 --> 00:27:11,190
- 别客气
- 快打开摄像机,动手吧
-You're welcome.
-Hidden cameras on, ready? Molest me.

422
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:14,090
- 快点啊,你得袭击我!
- 好吧!
-Molest me!
-You got it!

423
00:27:14,170 --> 00:27:16,160
- 天哪,救命!
- 来吧
-God, help!
-Give it to me.

424
00:27:16,330 --> 00:27:18,360
- 救命,抢劫啊!
- 好啊!
-Help, I'm being mugged!
-All right!

425
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:20,900
救命! 救命! 打劫啊!
Help! Help! I'm being mugged!

426
00:27:21,570 --> 00:27:24,060
- 够了!
- 祝你好运,回头办公室见
-Stop it!
-Good luck. See you at the office.

427
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:28,370
- 别担心,我会抓住他的
- 噢,老天!
-Don't worry, I'll get him.
-Oh, shit!

428
00:27:29,350 --> 00:27:30,440
站住
Stop right there.

429
00:27:36,020 --> 00:27:37,280
给我趴下!
Come on!

430
00:27:41,460 --> 00:27:43,090
兄弟,你是怎么搞的?
What's your problem, pal?

431
00:27:50,570 --> 00:27:51,660
起来
Come up here.

432
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:56,310
小姐,手袋帮你拿回来了,
老兄,找份正经工作吧
Got your pocketbook. Get a job, pal.

433
00:27:58,680 --> 00:27:59,800
小姐! 小姐!
Miss! Miss!

434
00:28:00,310 --> 00:28:03,080
- 你没事吧?
- 怎么回事?
-Are you okay?
-What happened?

435
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:04,510
我扶你起来
Let me help you up.

436
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,710
没事了,没事了
All right, now. All right.

437
00:28:13,590 --> 00:28:16,560
小姐你刚刚被纽约歹徒袭击
Ma'am, you were just the victim
of a New York City mugger.

438
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:19,450
我猜,那只不过是个小毛贼罢了
As I suspected, he was a coward and a weakling.

439
00:28:19,530 --> 00:28:22,290
竟然还满身香水味
And also wore more cologne
than any man should wear.

440
00:28:22,370 --> 00:28:24,930
- 我帮你把提包拿回来了
- 谢谢
-I got this back for you, though.
-Thank you.

441
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:29,140
- 要不要送你去医院?
- 不,不必了
-Can I take you to the hospital?
-No, no.

442
00:28:30,110 --> 00:28:34,540
我没事儿,只是有些头晕和受惊过度
I'll be all right.
I just feel a little dizzy and violated.

443
00:28:35,410 --> 00:28:36,740
我没事的
I'm fine.

444
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:42,150
别这样,你还是去医院看看吧
Please, let me take you to the emergency room.

445
00:28:43,550 --> 00:28:45,950
我真的没事,我只是...
I'm sure I'll be all right. I just need to...

446
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,490
...或者走走就行了....
...perhaps walk it off or....

447
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:50,490
- 能扶我一下么?
- 没问题
-Could you?
-Sure.

448
00:28:50,560 --> 00:28:51,620
谢谢你
Thank you.

449
00:28:52,830 --> 00:28:54,160
非常感谢
Thank you so much.

450
00:28:55,330 --> 00:28:58,000
我叫Pam. Pam Dawson.
My name is Pam. Pam Dawson.

451
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:02,870
我叫Deeds. 我不是本地人,来这儿旅游
My name is Deeds. I'm not from here.
I'm just visiting.

452
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,840
你从哪来?
Where do you hail from?

453
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:11,010
Mandrake山谷, 一个没多少人知道的小镇
在新安普郡
Mandrake Falls, New Hampshire.
Just a little town nobody's ever heard of.

454
00:29:11,620 --> 00:29:13,450
我也是从小镇来的
I'm from a little town like that.

455
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:17,250
- 在爱荷华
- 是吗? 在哪儿?
-In lowa.
-Is that right? What part?

456
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:21,880
Winchestertonfieldville
Winchestertonfieldville.

457
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:27,960
爱荷华州Winchestertonfieldville,一个小镇
Yes, the small town
of Winchestertonfieldville, lowa.

458
00:29:30,870 --> 00:29:32,060
对不起
I'm sorry.

459
00:29:32,140 --> 00:29:35,230
- 你来纽约干什么?
- 我在学校当护士
-What are you doing in New York?
-I'm a school nurse.

460
00:29:36,010 --> 00:29:39,940
- 你不可能是护士
- 为什么,你不相信吗?
-There's no way you're a school nurse.
-Why, don't you believe me?

461
00:29:40,410 --> 00:29:42,540
你这么好心,怎么可能是护士
You're too nice to be a school nurse.

462
00:29:43,050 --> 00:29:46,810
我学校的护士可恶极了,
每次我告诉她我胃疼...
My school nurse was so mean,
every time I'd tell her I had a tummy ache...

463
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:49,850
...她都会把我赶回教室,
命令我"不许哭哭啼啼"的!
...she'd send me back to my class
and say, "Stop whining."

464
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:52,690
- 真是太可怕了!
- 是啊,我天天都这么说!
-But that's awful!
-Well, I said it every day.

465
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,360
我很想念自己的妈妈
I missed my mother.

466
00:29:57,960 --> 00:29:59,290
多可爱!
That's sweet.

467
00:30:00,030 --> 00:30:01,120
Dawson小姐?
Miss Dawson?

468
00:30:01,870 --> 00:30:04,800
我在想,你是否愿意与我...
How would you like to maybe go out...

469
00:30:04,870 --> 00:30:07,240
...共进一个纽约式的晚餐?
...and have a New York City dinner with me?

470
00:30:07,770 --> 00:30:08,930
天哪！
Golly.

471
00:30:10,610 --> 00:30:12,410
听起来很不错
That sounds wonderful.

472
00:30:12,610 --> 00:30:14,040
- 是吗?
- 是的
-It does?
-Yeah.

473
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,740
- 那咱们去吧
- 好吧
-Let's do it, then.
-Okay.

474
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,080
去死吧，混蛋
Damn you, Old Spice.

475
00:30:23,550 --> 00:30:27,290
这么说你自己开了间批萨店，还喜欢写诗
So you run this pizza place
and you have your poetry.

476
00:30:28,290 --> 00:30:30,190
你来这儿只是为旅游?
What brings you to the big city?

477
00:30:30,260 --> 00:30:32,790
事实上，我刚刚继承了400亿美元遗产
Actually, I just inherited $40 billion.

478
00:30:33,900 --> 00:30:38,100
那可真不少, 但我总觉得那么大一笔钱
多少有些来路不正
Well, that's nice, but I think anything
over $30 billion is just gravy.

479
00:30:41,140 --> 00:30:42,370
有道理
I like that.

480
00:30:43,470 --> 00:30:46,380
你的金发真漂亮
Your hair is very blond and pretty.

481
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:49,740
我有瑞典学童
I'm of Swedish ancestry.

482
00:30:50,550 --> 00:30:52,070
- 是吗?
- 是
-Really?
-Yes.

483
00:30:52,980 --> 00:30:55,920
我祖父住在ABBA.
My grandfather was in ABBA.

484
00:30:57,390 --> 00:30:59,020
ABBA乐队?
ABBA, the band?

485
00:30:59,660 --> 00:31:03,490
劳驾, 有没有什么名人来这儿?
Excuse me,
do you get any famous people in here?

486
00:31:03,560 --> 00:31:04,960
什么大人物都有
Famous, rich, powerful.

487
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:07,900
是吗? 我们那儿可没什么名人
Really? We don't get
any famous people in Mandrake Falls.

488
00:31:07,970 --> 00:31:10,460
有一次,史蒂芬.金 路过我们的加油站...
Stephen King stopped by
our gas station one time...

489
00:31:10,530 --> 00:31:12,930
...但是竟然没人敢和他搭话
...but everyone was too scared to talk to him.

490
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,800
我想他一定很可怕
I'd imagine he'd be very spooky.

491
00:31:14,870 --> 00:31:18,270
加油站的员工Jake, 和他对望过一眼
Jake, the gas station attendant,
made eye contact with him.

492
00:31:18,340 --> 00:31:20,310
当晚体重就掉了200磅
That night he lost 200 pounds.

493
00:31:22,510 --> 00:31:23,500
Wow.
Wow.

494
00:31:24,450 --> 00:31:26,640
你们的奶酪烤鸡很快就好了
Your chicken parmesan should be ready soon.

495
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:30,950
好的,伙计 , 我看到
那边有一对夫妇在庆祝结婚周年
Okay, buddy. I saw a couple over there.
It's their anniversary.

496
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:34,390
把这个给他们,但别说是我们给的
Give them this. Don't say it's from us, though.

497
00:31:35,130 --> 00:31:36,590
这差不多有2万快呢!
This is like $20,000.

498
00:31:36,660 --> 00:31:40,100
就跟他们说,是餐厅酬宾活动之类的
谢了,伙计
Tell them it was a restaurant giveaway
or something. Thanks, buddy.

499
00:31:41,770 --> 00:31:45,200
这可是个花钱的好办法
That's an awfully nice way
to start spending your money.

500
00:31:45,270 --> 00:31:47,260
- 我不会认错人吧?
- 谁?
-Is that who I think it is?
-Who?

501
00:31:47,910 --> 00:31:50,770
Preston Blake的侄子, 身价400亿的那个
Preston Blake's nephew, the $40-billion man.

502
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:53,200
我们得会会他, Dave?
We have to meet him. Dave?

503
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:56,870
是吗, 那个歹徒没什么事儿就好
Gosh, I hope that mugger got home okay.

504
00:31:57,210 --> 00:31:58,580
- Deeds先生
- 什么事?
-Mr. Deeds.
-Yeah.

505
00:31:58,650 --> 00:32:01,680
Simonds先生想请您赏脸过去坐坐!
Mr. Simonds would like
to invite you to join his party.

506
00:32:02,250 --> 00:32:03,240
为什么?
Why is that?

507
00:32:03,820 --> 00:32:06,020
因为大家想一睹您女朋友的风采
Just to enjoy the pleasure of your company.

508
00:32:06,090 --> 00:32:08,120
是吗, 他可真有眼光
Wow, that's pretty cool of him.

509
00:32:12,500 --> 00:32:14,290
真是个热情的拥抱, Deeds.
That was a very nice hug, Deeds.

510
00:32:14,730 --> 00:32:18,000
非常感谢你的邀请, 我们非常高兴
It's wicked nice of you to invite us over.
This is awesome.

511
00:32:18,300 --> 00:32:21,360
- 我们在哪儿见过面吗?
- 我想没有,除非你的孩子生过病
-Have we met?
-Not unless you have a sick kid.

512
00:32:21,810 --> 00:32:25,040
您现在是城里的大人物了,Deeds先生
You're a very important man
in this town now, Mr. Deeds.

513
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:26,540
这我可不知道
I don't know about that.

514
00:32:26,610 --> 00:32:28,440
我在Metropolitan歌剧院工作...
I sing at the Metropolitan Opera...

515
00:32:28,510 --> 00:32:32,210
...我们百分之五十以上的经费
是由Blake媒体公司提供的
...and Blake Media contributes
50 percent of our budget.

516
00:32:32,280 --> 00:32:34,220
因此,我代表歌剧院:
So, on behalf of the opera:

517
00:32:34,290 --> 00:32:38,240
"感-谢-你"
"Thank you"

518
00:32:41,390 --> 00:32:42,720
唱得真好!
That was awesome!

519
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:46,320
不过你该感谢我叔公,而不是我
You shouldn't thank me, though.
You should thank my great-uncle.

520
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:47,800
他是个有趣的人
He was an interesting man.

521
00:32:47,870 --> 00:32:50,100
我和他在古根海姆委员会共事过
I served on the board
of the Guggenheim with him.

522
00:32:50,170 --> 00:32:53,100
是吗? 我可没听说过那个地方,
不过祝它好运
Really? I'm not sure what that is,
but good luck with it.

523
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:57,470
我很乐意为你在"纽约人"写篇文章
I'd love to write a piece on you
for The New Yorker.

524
00:32:57,540 --> 00:32:59,130
"纽约人"是什么?
What's The New Yorker?

525
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:01,170
是一份杂志
It's a magazine.

526
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:04,880
发表一些短评和讽刺漫画
With essays, witty cartoons.

527
00:33:05,580 --> 00:33:09,540
我经常看Mandrake的小报,
他们也登很多漫画
I read the Mandrake Falls Gazette
and they got some cartoons in there also.

528
00:33:09,620 --> 00:33:12,180
知道最有意思的是谁吗, 那个叫贝利的家伙
You know who's a riot? That Beetle Bailey guy.

529
00:33:12,290 --> 00:33:14,880
整天戴着顶帽子,到处惹事
He's always wearing his hat and doing his thing.

530
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:18,290
很荣幸见到了一位真正的作家, George.
But it is an honor to meet
a real writer like you, George.

531
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:20,800
我一直也想发表点东西...
I've been trying
to get my stuff published for years...

532
00:33:20,870 --> 00:33:23,300
... 但Hallmark的门槛实在太高了
...but Hallmark is one tough cookie to crack.

533
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:25,930
- Hallmark?
- 他喜欢写贺卡
-Hallmark?
-He writes greeting cards.

534
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:29,830
- 试试而已
- 您一定要让我们见识一下
-I try.
-You must share one with us.

535
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:33,500
- 我喜欢你的口音, "法国先生"
- 谁是"法国先生"?
-I don't know about that, Mr. French.
-Who's Mr. French?

536
00:33:33,580 --> 00:33:36,880
- 他象不像那个"法国先生"?
- 完全没听说过
-Doesn't he look like Mr. French?
-I've never heard of him.

537
00:33:36,950 --> 00:33:37,910
来嘛
Come on.

538
00:33:37,980 --> 00:33:39,610
好吧,就读一个吧
All right, I'll give you one.

539
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:42,310
这是我最近在写的一张母亲节贺卡
This is a Mother's Day card I've been working on.

540
00:33:42,390 --> 00:33:46,480
"老妈, 是你带我来到这个星球"
"Mom, you are the one
who brought me to planet Earth

541
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:50,490
"生我时你痛苦了14个钟头"
"You are the one who suffered
through my 14-hour birth

542
00:33:51,200 --> 00:33:55,150
"每次玩耍后,您把汽水送到我手中"
"You are the one who made lemonade for me
after I'd come back from play

543
00:33:55,570 --> 00:33:59,700
"我爱你,妈,愿您母亲节乐也融融"
"I love you, Mom,
so have a wicked nice Mother's Day"

544
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:01,600
就是这样了
Something like that.

545
00:34:02,410 --> 00:34:05,640
- 了不起的即兴创作!
-"天才,天才,天才"
-An instant classic!
-"Genius, genius, genius"

546
00:34:06,010 --> 00:34:08,040
你平时是用蜡笔写诗的吧?
Do you write your poems with a crayon?

547
00:34:12,380 --> 00:34:13,650
有意思!
It's amazing!

548
00:34:14,990 --> 00:34:17,750
我知道你们为什么请我们过来了,
想拿我寻开心,对吧?
I see why you brought me here.
To goof on me, huh?

549
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:20,880
- 别当真, Deeds.
- 闭嘴, George.
-Don't be silly, Deeds.
-Pipe down, George.

550
00:34:21,590 --> 00:34:24,460
对你们来说,我也许很可笑,
但如果你们到Mandrake去...
I may seem funny to you,
but if you came to Mandrake Falls...

551
00:34:24,530 --> 00:34:27,590
...可笑的会是你们,
但是却没人会嘲笑你们...
...you might seem funny to us.
Only nobody would laugh at you...

552
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:30,600
...令你们尴尬,
因为那不是待客之道!
...and make you feel stupid,
that wouldn't be good manners.

553
00:34:30,670 --> 00:34:34,260
也许我写的东西不怎么样,
但有些人很喜欢
Maybe my poems aren't that great,
but I know some people who like them.

554
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:38,470
不管怎么说,我尽力了,
我们要走了
Anyways, it's the best I can do.
We're going to get going.

555
00:34:38,540 --> 00:34:41,770
对不起,Pam.
希望你别在意!
Sorry about that, Pam.
I hope I didn't embarrass you.

556
00:34:46,780 --> 00:34:50,410
要不是Dawson 小姐在这儿,
我会好好收拾你们的
And if it wasn't for Miss Dawson being here,
I'd knock your heads in.

557
00:34:50,490 --> 00:34:51,680
我不介意
I don't mind.

558
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:52,980
那好吧
Okay.

559
00:34:56,660 --> 00:34:57,650
"不"
"No"

560
00:35:04,340 --> 00:35:08,240
我好像拉裤子了
I think I just shat myself.

561
00:35:09,110 --> 00:35:11,510
咱们去哪儿看风景?
How would you like to see the sights now?

562
00:35:11,580 --> 00:35:14,100
我先去补一补妆
I just need to powder my nose.

563
00:35:14,180 --> 00:35:16,580
好的,我帮你拿外套
That would be great. I'll get your coat.

564
00:35:17,210 --> 00:35:21,010
伙计们,这两万块算是赔偿你们的损失,
非常抱歉!
Hey, buddy, this will pay for everything
I damaged. Sorry about that.

565
00:35:21,090 --> 00:35:23,490
- 幸会了,各位
- 谢谢
-Good to meet you guys.
-Thank you.

566
00:35:23,550 --> 00:35:25,180
上帝, 千载难逢的机会
God, that was good stuff.

567
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:30,230
Mac,我要加薪
I want a raise, Mac.

568
00:35:34,670 --> 00:35:36,500
喂,兄弟,你好吗?
Hey, man! What's up?

569
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:39,200
老天爷啊, 你是John McEnroe(前网球明星)!
Holy cannoli, you're John McEnroe!

570
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:42,330
我看见你收拾那帮无礼的家伙,干得好!
I saw what you did to those guys
making fun of you. Nice work.

571
00:35:42,410 --> 00:35:45,380
有时候真是忍无可忍, 你明白的,对吧
Johnny Mac?
You know what it's like to get riled up
don't you, Johnny Mac?

572
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:48,280
- 我明白
- 我叫Deeds
-That I do.
-I'm Deeds, by the way.

573
00:35:48,350 --> 00:35:52,080
Deeds, 幸会了
去和我喝两杯吧
Deeds, nice to meet you.
You got to let me buy you a drink.

574
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:53,950
Dawson小姐, 这位是John McEnroe.
Miss Dawson, this is John McEnroe.

575
00:35:54,020 --> 00:35:57,680
- Dawson小姐, 很高兴见到你
- 我也是
-Miss Dawson, nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you, too.

576
00:35:57,890 --> 00:36:00,410
我答应陪Dawson小姐去观光
I promised Miss Dawson I'd take her sightseeing.

577
00:36:00,490 --> 00:36:03,760
这里风景不错,我很喜欢
The sights are great.
I've seen the sights. I love the sights.

578
00:36:03,830 --> 00:36:06,920
我带你们看看纽约不为人知的一面
Let me show you a New York
most people will never see.

579
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:10,800
- 你认为怎么样, Dawson小姐?
- 听起来挺有意思的!
-That okay with you, Miss Dawson?
-Sounds like fun!

580
00:36:10,870 --> 00:36:13,340
为狂欢之夜干杯!
Here's to a big night on the town.

581
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:27,480
发生什么事?
What happened?

582
00:36:27,580 --> 00:36:31,820
吃几片阿司匹林吧, Deeds先生
就不会那么头疼了
Here are some aspirins, Mr. Deeds.
They make your head seem smaller.

583
00:36:35,830 --> 00:36:38,990
- 我怎么换上睡衣了?
- 我帮您换的
-How did I get in these pajamas?
-I changed you.

584
00:36:39,530 --> 00:36:41,230
我很小心的,先生
I was very gentle, sir.

585
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:46,030
我猜,全曼哈顿的酒昨晚都让我喝光了!
I think I drank all the alcohol in Manhattan
last night.

586
00:36:46,340 --> 00:36:48,900
Dawson小姐也是这么说的
And you nearly succeeded,
according to Miss Dawson.

587
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:54,110
Dawson小姐! 我记得好像没送她回家, 她好吗?
Miss Dawson! I don't even remember
taking her home. Is she okay?

588
00:36:54,180 --> 00:36:57,240
我自己拿主意,用公司的车送她回去了
I took the liberty of sending her off
in the company limousine.

589
00:36:57,310 --> 00:37:00,250
她遇到麻烦,我帮了她
She was a lady in distress and I helped her.

590
00:37:00,850 --> 00:37:02,510
昨晚,我梦见她了
Dreamt about her last night.

591
00:37:03,050 --> 00:37:05,820
通常, 喝醉的人是不会做梦的
Usually, when you get blackout drunk
you don't dream.

592
00:37:07,390 --> 00:37:08,450
书上说的
So I read.

593
00:37:13,060 --> 00:37:14,390
什么事儿, Chuck?
What's up, Chuck?

594
00:37:17,900 --> 00:37:20,060
美国最新的亿万富翁...
America's newest billionaire...

595
00:37:21,770 --> 00:37:23,830
-...愚蠢的酒鬼
- 这是什么?
-...stupid and drunk.
-What's this?

596
00:37:23,910 --> 00:37:26,840
昨晚, Longfellow Deeds一定很尽兴
It was quite a night for Longfellow Deeds.

597
00:37:26,910 --> 00:37:29,500
他们现在知道我叫Longfellow了
They'll know my name is Longfellow.

598
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:32,350
殴打完几位社会名流之后...
After punching out some society types...

599
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:38,290
Deeds 又和"网球坏孩子" -- John McEnroe
混到了一块儿!
...Deeds joined forces with the original
bad boy of tennis, John McEnroe.

600
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:41,060
多么愚蠢的行径!
And stupidity won in straight sets.

601
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:49,730
他们是怎么拍到的?
How'd they get that footage?

602
00:37:50,230 --> 00:37:51,860
小心,Johnny!
Watch out, Johnny!

603
00:37:54,570 --> 00:37:57,730
你怎么开车的!
不知羞耻的家伙!
What kind of driving is that?
You're a fucking disgrace!

604
00:37:58,380 --> 00:38:00,370
不,先生. 你才不知羞耻!
No, sir. You're a disgrace.

605
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,780
- 太过瘾了, 兄弟!
- Johnny McEnroe!
-We did it, man!
-Johnny McEnroe!

606
00:38:02,850 --> 00:38:06,180
瞧啊, Deeds和McEnroe在一起!
太厉害了!
Look at Deedsy hanging out with McEnroe!
That's awesome!

607
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:08,810
是啊，我也很喜欢"沙滩小子"
I love the Beach Boys.

608
00:38:09,550 --> 00:38:11,680
Here I go, here I go.

609
00:38:14,430 --> 00:38:17,120
你这种表现可不是我们现在所需要的
This is not the kind of attention
we need right now.

610
00:38:17,290 --> 00:38:18,390
什么意思?
What do you mean?

611
00:38:18,460 --> 00:38:21,330
目前来说,你是我们最大的股东...
For the moment you're the largest stockholder...

612
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,960
...你的这种行为...
...and people might think
any instability you show...

613
00:38:24,030 --> 00:38:26,200
...将会直接影响公司的稳定
...may equal instability in the company.

614
00:38:30,270 --> 00:38:31,260
是我的错
My bad.

615
00:38:33,310 --> 00:38:35,570
是我的错,是我的错
My bad. My bad.

616
00:38:35,650 --> 00:38:36,640
好了,好了
Okay. Okay.

617
00:38:36,710 --> 00:38:37,700
- 是我的错
- 没事的
-My bad.
-Okay.

618
00:38:37,850 --> 00:38:41,050
需要我帮您叫车去葬礼吗 ? Cedar先生
Shall I call your car, Mr. Cedar,
to take you to the funeral?

619
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:42,450
什么葬礼?
What funeral?

620
00:38:43,350 --> 00:38:45,010
你叔公的
Your great-uncle's funeral.

621
00:38:45,090 --> 00:38:47,060
- 是今天?
- 是的
-His funeral's today?
-Today, yes.

622
00:38:47,420 --> 00:38:49,190
我去穿衣服
I'll go get my suit on.

623
00:38:56,700 --> 00:38:58,830
- 听着,多嘴的东西
- 先生?
-Cute, bigmouth.
-Sir?

624
00:38:59,270 --> 00:39:01,570
那个白痴一回到乡下...
As soon as that moron goes back
to Cowpie Falls...

625
00:39:01,640 --> 00:39:04,370
你这个波多黎各笨蛋也给我滚！
...you are out of here
on your fat Puerto Rican ass.

626
00:39:09,310 --> 00:39:11,040
我来自西班牙,先生
I hail from Spain, sir.

627
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:18,450
Ol?
Ol?

628
00:39:19,860 --> 00:39:23,920
"此刻, Preston弟兄必在天际飞翔"
Now, Brother Preston is soaring
with eagles high above.

629
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:27,790
"只因,一生爱心不停释放"
Because he lived a life of love.

630
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:32,230
"他如今高高在上..."
Yes, he's flying way up high...

631
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:35,760
"...无人会将他遗忘"
...because he was a supercool guy.

632
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:40,470
"伟大的生命匆匆逝去..."
He's gone away, too soon, it seems...

633
00:39:41,110 --> 00:39:44,010
"未完的事业何人承继"
...leaving behind his unfinished dreams.

634
00:39:44,380 --> 00:39:47,110
这位老兄写贺卡肯定能发大财!
This guy could make a fortune
writing greeting cards.

635
00:39:47,180 --> 00:39:50,020
"我们的朋友Preston Blake..."
Yes, we remember Preston Blake...

636
00:39:50,550 --> 00:39:53,390
信念坚定,无人能移!
...a man with faith no man could shake.

637
00:39:54,220 --> 00:39:56,390
胆识超群,无人能敌!
A strength no man could break.

638
00:39:56,930 --> 00:39:59,420
品格优良,无人能比!
A character no man could fake.

639
00:40:00,230 --> 00:40:02,790
上帝保佑,愿他安息!
For goodness sake, let's eat some cake.

640
00:40:03,170 --> 00:40:04,630
阿门
Amen.

641
00:40:06,540 --> 00:40:09,510
请留步, 牧师, 您说的太精彩了
Excuse me, Reverend, that was a grand slam.

642
00:40:09,570 --> 00:40:12,510
"在天际翱翔"那段简直太感人了
That part with soaring with the eagles
gave me goosebumps.

643
00:40:12,580 --> 00:40:16,100
- 谢谢你,兄弟
- 我生日那天,朋友们送了个啤酒杯给我
-Thank you, my brother.
-My friend got me a mug for my birthday.

644
00:40:16,180 --> 00:40:20,010
上面写着 "未能展翅高飞,只因鹤立鸡群"
It says, "It's hard to soar with the eagles
when you're surrounded by turkeys."

645
00:40:20,080 --> 00:40:21,810
但还是你的诗更好
But what you said was better.

646
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:23,520
都很好
It's all good.

647
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:27,820
安息吧, Preston.
让我们结束今天的仪式
Rest in peace, Preston.
That concludes today's service.

648
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:31,690
我还想说两句
I actually thought I would say something.

649
00:40:33,460 --> 00:40:36,060
Deeds的口才是学校里最好的
Deedsy was always the best speaker in school.

650
00:40:36,830 --> 00:40:37,700
Deeds?
Deedsy?

651
00:40:37,770 --> 00:40:39,930
只是顺便说几句,阁下
That's some job, by the way, Your Majesty.

652
00:40:40,270 --> 00:40:42,260
我们不是在看"史酷比"吗 ?
I thought we were watching Scooby-Doo.

653
00:40:43,110 --> 00:40:47,270
Hi, 我是 Deeds.
Preston Blake是我的叔公
Hi, my name is Deeds.
I was Preston Blake's great-nephew.

654
00:40:47,680 --> 00:40:51,010
在来这儿的路上, 我做了一首诗献给他
I wrote a poem for him
on my way over here, in my head.

655
00:40:51,350 --> 00:40:53,780
请允许我为大家朗诵
And I'm going to recite it for you.

656
00:40:54,450 --> 00:40:58,440
当然,它和Sharpton牧师的大作无法相比
I didn't realize I'd be following
the rhyme-master Reverend Sharpton.

657
00:40:58,890 --> 00:41:00,520
但我还是想和大家分享
But here we go anyways.

658
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:04,090
"你攀登高山,建造大楼"
"You climbed mountains and built skyscrapers

659
00:41:05,300 --> 00:41:09,200
"创办报纸,还有精彩的TV-SHOW"
"You made TV shows and put out newspapers

660
00:41:10,870 --> 00:41:13,460
"摆弄股票,你最拿手"
"You were wicked good at doing stocks

661
00:41:14,610 --> 00:41:17,070
"你喜欢,有仆人侍侯左右"
"You liked it
when Emilio would change your socks

662
00:41:18,740 --> 00:41:21,540
"可惜未能与你相处, 哪怕一分一秒"
"We never hung out and that makes me sad

663
00:41:22,410 --> 00:41:24,740
"不然,日子该有多美好"
"AII the good times we could've had"

664
00:41:25,450 --> 00:41:26,880
不错,很压韵
Nice rhyme.

665
00:41:27,350 --> 00:41:30,810
"我去世时,您不该把泪掉"
"But when I die, Uncle Preston,
you'd better say, 'Cheers!'

666
00:41:31,590 --> 00:41:34,250
"因为你我在天堂相会"
"'Cause me and you are hanging
at the pearly gates

667
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:38,260
"多么美妙,多么美妙!"
"I'll bring the beers, I'll bring the beers"

668
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:40,020
写得不错!
He's good.

669
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:41,590
Amen.
Amen.

670
00:41:41,670 --> 00:41:45,330
或许是你们的习俗,但在我们那儿
I know this is supposed to be
a closed casket, but where I come from...

671
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:49,070
...一般会打开棺材,以便大家能看见遗体,
追思凭吊...
...we feel it's good to see the body
for the grieving process, so....

672
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:55,030
抱歉各位,我看还是盖上吧!
Sorry about that! I'll keep this sucker closed.

673
00:41:59,820 --> 00:42:01,650
他还冻得硬邦邦的
He's still pretty frozen.

674
00:42:02,290 --> 00:42:03,510
差不多了
Almost there.

675
00:42:05,790 --> 00:42:08,220
我会帮你照料公司的, 我爱你
I'll keep an eye on the company for you.
Love you.

676
00:42:08,290 --> 00:42:10,490
很高兴见到你,多谢你的大房子
Nice meeting you. Thanks for the apartment.

677
00:42:11,030 --> 00:42:12,220
真疯狂
That was freaky.

678
00:42:12,730 --> 00:42:14,290
各位走好!
Everybody drive home safe.

679
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:16,690
嘿! 这家伙真是古怪
Man, this guy is in way over his head.

680
00:42:16,770 --> 00:42:18,930
- 你自己小心点
- 今晚约了他 ?
-Take care.
-You'll see him tonight?

681
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:22,340
是的,我4点钟给他打电话,
然后就准备开工
Yes, I'm calling around 4:00.
That's when I get off work.

682
00:42:22,570 --> 00:42:28,170
别忘了, 我是Pam Dawson, 纯洁的少女,
来自Winchestertonfieldville的护士小姐
Remember, I'm Pam Dawson, virgin school nurse
from Winchestertonfieldville, lowa.

683
00:42:30,610 --> 00:42:31,810
真有你的!
That's priceless.

684
00:42:33,450 --> 00:42:34,540
你,纯洁? 哈哈哈 !
You, a virgin.

685
00:42:34,540 --> 00:42:35,770
你,纯洁? 哈哈哈 !

686
00:42:41,220 --> 00:42:43,750
- 好的,谢谢你
- 先生,你这是 ?
-All right, thank you.
-Excuse me, sir.

687
00:42:44,160 --> 00:42:46,600
- 是我让他拿的
- 多谢了,Deeds.
-I told him he could have that.
-Thanks.

688
00:42:46,660 --> 00:42:48,260
别客气,伙计. 幸会了
Right on. Nice seeing you.

689
00:42:48,530 --> 00:42:51,330
随时欢迎你来用洗手间,知道吗?
You need to use our bathroom,
come back and use it, okay?

690
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:53,370
- 好的,Deeds.!
-Will do!
-All right.

691
00:42:54,840 --> 00:42:57,000
今天葬礼上我的表现怎么样?
How do you think I did at the funeral today?

692
00:42:57,070 --> 00:42:58,600
你的话很感人,先生
You spoke beautifully, sir.

693
00:42:59,040 --> 00:43:00,170
我还是有些过意不去
I still feel bad.

694
00:43:00,240 --> 00:43:03,940
我把叔公的胳膊给掰断了
I snapped my uncle's hand off
when I put him back in the casket.

695
00:43:04,410 --> 00:43:06,350
还好,他已经死了, 先生.
Lucky for him, he was dead, sir.

696
00:43:06,850 --> 00:43:09,280
很奇怪,即使他的脸冻成那个样子...
Even though his face was frozen that way...

697
00:43:09,790 --> 00:43:12,620
...可我觉得他还是很快乐,对不对?
...it looked to me like he was a happy guy.
Am I right?

698
00:43:13,120 --> 00:43:15,820
- 他是这样的
- 来,陪我坐坐
-He truly was.
-Come on, sit down, please.

699
00:43:16,330 --> 00:43:19,780
他天天都是这样...
And I got to hang out with him, just like this...

700
00:43:20,300 --> 00:43:22,420
...我们相处了差不多30年
...almost every day for 30 years.

701
00:43:22,930 --> 00:43:24,660
你们都聊些什么话题?
What did you guys talk about?

702
00:43:24,740 --> 00:43:28,900
人生,爱情,艺术,生意之类的
We spoke of life, love, art, wine, business.

703
00:43:29,310 --> 00:43:31,000
他令我获益良多
I learned much from him.

704
00:43:31,310 --> 00:43:33,240
- 你一定很怀念他
- 是的
-I bet you miss him, too.
-I do.

705
00:43:33,640 --> 00:43:35,580
他就像我父亲一样
He was like a parent to me.

706
00:43:36,310 --> 00:43:39,410
你知道的,我没见过自己的父亲,而母亲...
You see, I never knew my father, and Mama...

707
00:43:39,980 --> 00:43:42,470
我刚出生她就去世了
...she passed while giving the birth to me.

708
00:43:45,720 --> 00:43:47,990
- 想来点可可豆么?
- 不了,谢谢
-You want some Cocoa Pebbles?
-No, thanks.

709
00:43:48,890 --> 00:43:52,190
我还有很多活要干
I have much work to do.

710
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:55,800
- 谢谢你,不用了
- 慢慢吃
-Thanks. You don't have to do that.
-Enjoy your Pebbles.

711
00:43:57,170 --> 00:43:58,600
还有一件事
One more thing.

712
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:02,640
你叔公也没让我给它换袜子
Your great-uncle did not let me
change his socks for him, either.

713
00:44:03,770 --> 00:44:05,040
我喜欢脚
I like feet.

714
00:44:06,010 --> 00:44:07,200
不知为什么!
I do not know why.

715
00:44:15,850 --> 00:44:16,720
喂?
Hello.

716
00:44:16,790 --> 00:44:19,450
你好,是Deeds么? 我是Pam, Pam Dawson.
Hi, Deeds? It's Pam. Pam Dawson.

717
00:44:19,690 --> 00:44:23,720
你能来电话太好了! 昨晚的事我非常抱歉
I'm so happy you called.
I'm wicked sorry about last night.

718
00:44:23,790 --> 00:44:25,190
我不常喝酒
I don't drink very often.

719
00:44:25,460 --> 00:44:28,360
你酒量不错嘛
I thought you held your liquor very well.

720
00:44:28,430 --> 00:44:30,760
可惜还是吐了你一身!
Unfortunately, I couldn't hold it for too long.

721
00:44:30,930 --> 00:44:34,530
别在意,反正那条裙子我也不是太喜欢
That's okay. I didn't really like that skirt anyway.

722
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:39,300
又有一个电话进来,
能麻烦你等一等吗?
I'm getting a call on the other line.
Can you hang on for a second?

723
00:44:39,380 --> 00:44:41,040
- 没问题
- 谢谢
-Sure.
-Thank you.

724
00:44:41,710 --> 00:44:42,540
喂
Hello.

725
00:44:42,610 --> 00:44:45,710
Deeds先生, 我是Kevin Ward,
就是上次你揍的那个四分卫
Mr. Deeds, this is Kevin Ward,
the quarterback you punched.

726
00:44:46,180 --> 00:44:47,450
噢,我想起来了,什么事儿,朋友?
What's up, buddy?

727
00:44:47,780 --> 00:44:52,720
我反覆考虑过了,我不该那样目中无人,
I wanted to say that I was thinking it over
and I'd like to live up to my word.

728
00:44:52,990 --> 00:44:54,790
我希望能帮您赢得超级杯
And I'd like to win you a Super Bowl.

729
00:44:54,860 --> 00:44:57,490
- 那太好了,伙计
- 我爸想和您说两句
-That's terrific, pal.
-And my daddy wants to speak to you.

730
00:44:58,930 --> 00:45:01,020
Deeds. 我是Buddy Ward, Kevin的父亲
Deeds. Buddy Ward here, Kevin's daddy.

731
00:45:01,330 --> 00:45:02,420
你好吗, Ward先生?
How you doing, Mr. Ward?

732
00:45:02,670 --> 00:45:05,070
我想感谢你给我儿子上了一课
I just want to thank you
for teaching my boy a lesson.

733
00:45:05,140 --> 00:45:09,040
他是个好孩子,只是
在女士面前说话时要文明一些
He's a good kid. He just has to watch
his language in front of ladies.

734
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:13,800
我会提醒Kevin,是谁生他出来的
I'll remind Kevin where he comes from.

735
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:15,710
那太好了
That sounds terrific.

736
00:45:15,980 --> 00:45:19,110
你在女士面前说脏话?
You used foul language in front of a lady?

737
00:45:19,880 --> 00:45:20,910
别打我,爸,别打我!
No, Daddy, no!

738
00:45:25,260 --> 00:45:25,980
Pam
Pam.

739
00:45:26,460 --> 00:45:27,390
我听着呢
Still here.

740
00:45:27,720 --> 00:45:28,990
你在干什么呢,上班?
How's it going? You at work?

741
00:45:29,430 --> 00:45:32,590
- 是的, 我现在在医疗室
- 有"顾客"吗?
-Yep, here in the nurse's office.
-Any customers?

742
00:45:33,400 --> 00:45:35,560
顾客? 噢,你是说生病的孩子
Customers? Oh, sick kids.

743
00:45:36,500 --> 00:45:39,830
恩, 小Billy在这儿
Well, little Billy Barty's here.

744
00:45:40,670 --> 00:45:45,660
- 你哪儿不舒服, Billy?
- Dawson小姐, 我肚子疼
-You're not feeling too good, Billy?
-Miss Dawson, my tummy hurts.

745
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:48,440
你可以试试安静的躺一会儿
Why don't you just lay back and relax?

746
00:45:49,080 --> 00:45:50,570
你干得不错
That was nice. Good job.

747
00:45:50,750 --> 00:45:54,480
我拉屎屎了
I've got too much doo-doo in my underpants.

748
00:45:55,590 --> 00:45:57,880
臭死了
Make the stinky go away.

749
00:45:58,290 --> 00:46:01,120
看来你要忙一阵子了...
Well, you sound like
you got your hands full, so...

750
00:46:01,320 --> 00:46:03,090
...我还是直说了吧
...I'll just come out with it.

751
00:46:03,590 --> 00:46:06,080
我今晚想约你出来,你愿意吗?
How would you like
to do something with me tonight?

752
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:08,730
我很愿意
I'd love to do something with you.

753
00:46:08,970 --> 00:46:09,860
太好了
Great.

754
00:46:10,070 --> 00:46:12,730
不过不能去喝酒, 免得给公司惹麻烦
We can't go out drinking.
I got our company in trouble.

755
00:46:12,800 --> 00:46:16,430
好的, 从小家里人就教育我不要喝酒
That's okay.
I was brought up never to drink alcohol.

756
00:46:17,140 --> 00:46:19,110
连酒心糖也别吃
Not even rum raisin ice cream.

757
00:46:19,380 --> 00:46:21,710
没错, 咱们去干点别的吧
I like that. I'll think of something good.

758
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:23,410
今晚见
See you tonight.

759
00:46:23,680 --> 00:46:24,670
好的,再见
Okay. 'Bye.

760
00:46:28,820 --> 00:46:30,340
我得试试这个
I got to try this.

761
00:46:43,230 --> 00:46:44,560
有意思吧?
Was that awesome?

762
00:46:46,300 --> 00:46:47,930
上垒还是出局?
Am I out or safe?

763
00:46:49,770 --> 00:46:51,240
明白!
I'm with you.

764
00:46:53,180 --> 00:46:56,840
这是什么? 我叔公的日记!
What is this? My great-uncle's personal journal.

765
00:46:58,380 --> 00:47:00,850
- 我能看么?
- 自家人
-Should I read it?
-Family.

766
00:47:02,590 --> 00:47:04,380
没错,自家人,没问题
Family, safe, good.

767
00:47:04,790 --> 00:47:08,450
好吧,晚安! 我后背疼死了!
All right, have a good night. My back hurts!

768
00:47:13,300 --> 00:47:15,700
- 很高兴和你们交易
- 谢谢你,Deeds先生
-Nice doing business with you.
-Thank you.

769
00:47:15,770 --> 00:47:17,320
谢谢你们的自行车
Thanks for the bikes.

770
00:47:17,400 --> 00:47:19,890
这两万块你打算怎么花?
What are you gonna do with your $20,000?

771
00:47:19,970 --> 00:47:22,800
买冰激凌.
你呢?
Buy a giraffe.
What are you gonna do with your $20,000?

772
00:47:22,870 --> 00:47:24,340
退学
Quit school.

773
00:47:24,410 --> 00:47:28,570
好主意,傻瓜才去上学,你们看看我!
Good idea, school is for fools. Look at me!

774
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:55,900
这公园真美
The park is beautiful.

775
00:47:56,810 --> 00:48:00,400
这些树有没有让你想起Winchestertonfieldville?
These trees, they remind you
of Winchestertonfieldville at all?

776
00:48:01,510 --> 00:48:03,840
是啊,当然,我想起了很多
Oh, yes. Very much so.

777
00:48:04,510 --> 00:48:06,640
在那里的生活很有意思吧?
What was it like growing up there?

778
00:48:06,780 --> 00:48:07,910
非常有意思
It was great.

779
00:48:08,750 --> 00:48:12,520
我还记得那时到街角的杂货铺...
I remember walking down
to the corner drugstore...

780
00:48:12,590 --> 00:48:14,890
...买麦芽糖奶昔
...and getting malted milkshakes.

781
00:48:15,990 --> 00:48:17,790
你家的房子什么样?
What was your house like?

782
00:48:18,260 --> 00:48:20,560
很大,维多利亚式的
We had this big Victorian.

783
00:48:21,260 --> 00:48:22,960
在大街的右边
Right off Main Street.

784
00:48:24,170 --> 00:48:27,930
- 蓝色的百叶窗, 大门是红色的
- 真不错
-Blue shutters and a big red door.
-All right.

785
00:48:28,470 --> 00:48:32,410
- 屋前的院子里有一架秋千
- 太可爱了
-And a tire swing in the front yard.
-I love it.

786
00:48:32,840 --> 00:48:37,400
记得那次我从老Radley的苹果树上摔下来...
And I remember the time I fell out of
old Boo Radley's apple tree...

787
00:48:37,510 --> 00:48:38,880
...把胳膊给摔断了
...and broke my arm.

788
00:48:39,580 --> 00:48:43,990
我父亲, 那时他还没有...
And my father, before he passed away...

789
00:48:44,420 --> 00:48:46,690
死于麻风病
...from the disease of the lepers...

790
00:48:46,760 --> 00:48:51,090
...他抱起我,一直跑到Pepper大夫家
...he came and he scooped me up
and he ran me all the way to Dr. Pepper's.

791
00:48:52,730 --> 00:48:53,890
Pepper大夫
Dr. Pepper.

792
00:48:54,730 --> 00:48:55,720
是的
Yeah.

793
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:57,730
还好有他
I'm glad that guy was around.

794
00:48:58,740 --> 00:49:00,900
- 想坐一会儿吗?
- 好的
-Want to sit down?
-Sure.

795
00:49:02,940 --> 00:49:04,410
- 谢谢你
- 乐意效劳
-Thank you.
-My pleasure.

796
00:49:05,180 --> 00:49:08,630
在来的路上,我一直在读叔公的日记
I was reading my great-uncle's journal
on my way over to you.

797
00:49:08,710 --> 00:49:10,980
他9岁时写道...
And, when he was age 9...

798
00:49:11,050 --> 00:49:14,810
他们是唯一有收音机的家庭...
...he wrote that he had the only family
on the block with a radio...

799
00:49:14,880 --> 00:49:17,820
...他梦想将来能成为一名DJ(音乐主持人)
...and he was dreaming
of becoming a disc jockey someday.

800
00:49:17,890 --> 00:49:20,220
DJ?
A disc jockey?

801
00:49:22,530 --> 00:49:25,790
知道吗,我小时候一直梦想能成为记者
You know, when I was a kid,
I wanted to be a news reporter.

802
00:49:26,860 --> 00:49:29,590
经常到处去采访别人...
I used to go around interviewing everyone...

803
00:49:29,670 --> 00:49:32,500
...然后在自己的小本子上写呀、写呀
...and writing notes
in my little Holly Hobby notebook.

804
00:49:34,640 --> 00:49:37,900
弄得别人很讨厌，结果捱了不少揍
People didn't like that. I got beat up a lot.

805
00:49:38,070 --> 00:49:42,030
- 还记得打你的家伙吗?
- 忘了,那是很久以前了
-Do you remember their names?
-No, it was a long time ago.

806
00:49:43,180 --> 00:49:44,940
但我奶奶却对我说:
But my grandma said to me:

807
00:49:45,320 --> 00:49:48,550
"总有一天你会成为大记者...
"One day you'll grow up
and work for 60 Minutes...

808
00:49:48,620 --> 00:49:50,710
"...改变这个世界"
"...and make a difference in the world."

809
00:49:51,620 --> 00:49:55,180
你每天都在改变着这个世界, 你是孩子们的好护士
You do make a difference in the world,
every day. You're a school nurse.

810
00:49:58,830 --> 00:50:00,990
对了,还有一件事是关于我叔公的
Anyways, this is what happened to my uncle.

811
00:50:01,060 --> 00:50:05,260
在他晚年那段日子, 他会每天早上3点钟...
Later on in his life, he'd go
to this radio station that he owned...

812
00:50:05,340 --> 00:50:08,270
到自己的电台, 做一个小时的DJ
...at 3:00 in the morning and DJ for an hour.

813
00:50:08,340 --> 00:50:09,600
太有意思了
That's great.

814
00:50:10,610 --> 00:50:13,770
所以,别放弃自己的愿望,
你会成为记者的
So, don't give up hope.
You'll be a reporter someday.

815
00:50:14,340 --> 00:50:15,940
只要你不放弃
If you really want to.

816
00:50:17,410 --> 00:50:19,010
是那样就好了
That would be nice.

817
00:50:22,120 --> 00:50:24,250
- 不好,着火了!
- 着火?
-Jeesum Crow, a fire!
-A fire?

818
00:50:24,750 --> 00:50:26,620
- 我们得去帮忙
- 我们?
-We should help.
-We should?

819
00:50:26,690 --> 00:50:28,620
- 咱们走
- 去着火那里?
-Let's get going.
-To the fire?

820
00:50:29,260 --> 00:50:32,920
- Fifi, 到这儿来
- 跳啊,我们会接住你的
-Fifi, get over here right now.
-Come on, we'll catch you.

821
00:50:33,260 --> 00:50:36,490
走开, 我不能丢下我的小猫,
它们是我唯一的亲人
Go away! I can't leave without my kitties.
They're all I got.

822
00:50:37,870 --> 00:50:38,770
她发疯了!
Crazy lady!

823
00:50:38,840 --> 00:50:41,860
- 噢,小乖乖,你们在哪儿?
- 上去,快!
-Oh, babies, where are you?
-Up there now, get going!

824
00:50:42,170 --> 00:50:46,840
我是Longfellow Deeds, Mandrake镇的
义务消防局长. 我这就上去!
Longfellow Deeds, Mandrake Falls
volunteer fire chief. I'll be up there in a jiff.

825
00:50:46,910 --> 00:50:49,570
- 他发疯了
- 竟然要上去!
-He's crazy.
-He's going up there right now, though.

826
00:50:50,080 --> 00:50:52,170
- 小心,伙计!
- 他要干什么?
-Look at him.
-Where's he going?

827
00:50:53,220 --> 00:50:54,410
瞧啊!
Watch it, man!

828
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:57,240
- Sully, 那个家伙是谁?
- 我不知道
-Sully, who's that guy up there?
-I don't know.

829
00:50:57,320 --> 00:50:59,950
他说他是Mandrake消防局的
He says he's from
the Mandrake Falls Fire Department.

830
00:51:01,220 --> 00:51:04,790
- 老天,这是什么功夫啊?
- 简直是人猿泰山的亲戚
-How's he climb like that?
-He must have monkey blood in him.

831
00:51:04,890 --> 00:51:07,520
和纽约最勇敢的人并肩战斗
是我的荣幸!
It's an honor to work
with New York's bravest guys.

832
00:51:07,630 --> 00:51:09,000
小心!
Be careful!

833
00:51:09,070 --> 00:51:12,470
- 我来救你了
- 小乖乖,你们在哪啊?
-I'll get you.
-Babies, where are you?

834
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:14,800
- 女士!
- 老天,太热了
-Ma'am!
-Lord, it's hot in here.

835
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:18,370
- 小猫咪,到妈妈这儿来
- 请别慌,会没事儿的
-Kitties, come to Mommy.
-Calm down. Everything will be all right.

836
00:51:18,440 --> 00:51:20,710
好吧, 但我决不会丢下我的猫
Okay, but I'm not leaving without my kitties.

837
00:51:20,780 --> 00:51:22,340
- 一共几只?
- 7只.
-How many do you got?
-Seven.

838
00:51:22,650 --> 00:51:24,670
真他妈的多, 快开始找吧!
Holy shit! Let's get cracking.

839
00:51:26,420 --> 00:51:28,980
- 抱歉说粗话
- 接受你的道歉
-I apologize for the language.
-Apology accepted.

840
00:51:33,990 --> 00:51:36,650
- 火灾让我兴奋
- 别客气,尽情享受!
-Fire excites me.
-Knock yourself out.

841
00:51:38,600 --> 00:51:40,860
- 过来
- 那个是Freddy.
-Come here.
-That's Freddy.

842
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:44,690
- 下去吧!
- 不,我的孩子!
-Here we go!
-Oh, my children!

843
00:51:50,840 --> 00:51:53,710
- 接的好, Pam!
- 你扔的也不错, Deeds!
-Nice catch, Pam!
-Good throw, Deeds!

844
00:52:04,890 --> 00:52:08,380
- 那是Frobo. 谢谢你
- 来了,伙计们
-That's Frobo. Thank you, darling.
-Coming at you, boys.

845
00:52:12,330 --> 00:52:13,660
让我来!
I'll take that.

846
00:52:14,460 --> 00:52:16,730
- 还有几只呢
- Okay, okay.
-There's a lot more.
-Okay, okay.

847
00:52:28,950 --> 00:52:30,670
老天爷, 一只猫!
Holy shit, it's a cat!

848
00:52:34,420 --> 00:52:36,580
好一个长传. 我来了,猫咪
Full snap. I got you, kitty.

849
00:52:39,160 --> 00:52:40,490
接的漂亮!
Nice grab!

850
00:52:41,960 --> 00:52:43,150
还有一只
One more to go.

851
00:52:43,690 --> 00:52:45,820
Fifi, 你在哪儿?
Fifi, where are you?

852
00:52:47,060 --> 00:52:50,060
- 我找到Fifi了
- Oh, 太好了!
-I think I found Fifi.
-Oh, good!

853
00:52:50,930 --> 00:52:52,800
坚持住,小兄弟!
Hang in there, buddy!

854
00:52:54,300 --> 00:52:55,530
我来,我来!
I got it!

855
00:53:03,280 --> 00:53:05,180
来吧,咱们一起跳
Okay, let's do this together.

856
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:07,970
小心啊!
Be careful!

857
00:53:08,050 --> 00:53:10,450
别担心,这对他们是小菜一碟
All right, they do it all the time. Here we go.

858
00:53:14,120 --> 00:53:15,220
Oh,天哪!
Oh, shit!

859
00:53:18,760 --> 00:53:19,750
Deeds.
Deeds.

860
00:53:20,300 --> 00:53:21,630
我没事
I'm okay.

861
00:53:22,170 --> 00:53:23,290
你没事吧?
Are you okay?

862
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:26,930
是的,太谢谢你了!
Yes, I am. Thanks to you!

863
00:53:29,340 --> 00:53:30,670
救命啊!
You're hurting me!

864
00:53:34,940 --> 00:53:37,140
Longfellow Deeds又在生事了
Longfellow Deeds is at it again.

865
00:53:37,810 --> 00:53:39,940
Coretta Keeling女士成了他受害者...
His latest victim, Coretta Keeling...

866
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:42,810
...她非常爱自己的小猫咪
...whose only crime
was loving her cats too much.

867
00:53:42,890 --> 00:53:45,150
不幸,被Deeds知道了
And letting Deeds find out about it.

868
00:53:45,460 --> 00:53:47,790
- 我来了!
- 走开!
-I'll get you!
-Go away!

869
00:53:48,590 --> 00:53:50,580
- 真绝了
- 两个一起来!
-I love it.
-Here comes two!

870
00:53:53,430 --> 00:53:56,690
- 杀害猫咪的凶手!
- 害死了可爱的猫咪之后...
-Cat killer!
-After he finished with her cats...

871
00:53:56,770 --> 00:53:59,500
...他又把手伸向了Keeling小姐
...he turned his sights on Miss Keeling herself.

872
00:54:01,900 --> 00:54:03,130
上帝!
My God!

873
00:54:03,710 --> 00:54:05,040
我拍的不是这样
That's not what I shot.

874
00:54:05,110 --> 00:54:07,670
这位Longfellow受到任何惩罚了吗? 没有!
当然不会!
Has Longfellow Deeds been locked up?
Of course not.

875
00:54:07,910 --> 00:54:12,040
我们所遵守的法律在这些公子哥儿眼中,
只是一个玩笑罢了
While the rest of us obey the law,
rich playboys like himself get to laugh at it.

876
00:54:14,020 --> 00:54:17,450
这就是Longfellow Deeds---本周最愚蠢的傻瓜
Longfellow Deeds. Our jackass of the week.

877
00:54:18,350 --> 00:54:20,650
到底是谁? 是谁编辑了带子
What the hell? Who edited that?

878
00:54:20,990 --> 00:54:25,320
是我, 你做的那个版本非常好,
但我需要更夸张一点
I did. Your first cut was great,
but I needed to spice it up a bit.

879
00:54:25,630 --> 00:54:27,560
事实上那是一个多好的素材啊!
The truth was a great story.

880
00:54:27,930 --> 00:54:30,920
他救了那个女人和她的7只小猫
He saved that woman and her seven cats.

881
00:54:31,230 --> 00:54:33,930
- 他是个英雄!
- 英雄是不错
-He was heroic!
-Heroic is nice.

882
00:54:34,200 --> 00:54:36,570
- 但堕落和疯狂更有观众
-Depraved and insane is better.
-Hell, yeah!

883
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:40,640
这片子是你拍的,干得好,
继续努力!
This footage you're getting, gorgeous.
Keep it coming!

884
00:54:41,740 --> 00:54:44,270
天哪,我们怎么能这样对一个好人?
God, how can we do this to such a sweet guy?

885
00:54:44,350 --> 00:54:46,370
好人? 好人?
Sweet? Sweet?

886
00:54:47,120 --> 00:54:48,580
瞧瞧我!
Look at me!

887
00:54:48,650 --> 00:54:52,020
他暴揍我那时,像个好人吗?
Was he sweet when he gave me
the most savage beating of my life?

888
00:54:52,290 --> 00:54:54,590
- 可你是歹徒啊!
- Babe!
-You were mugging me!
-Babe!

889
00:54:55,430 --> 00:54:58,720
相信我,世界上没有那么好的人!
No one is as good as this guy's pretending to be.

890
00:54:59,360 --> 00:55:00,850
别傻了!
Don't be a sucker.

891
00:55:01,500 --> 00:55:03,090
不该这么对他的
He doesn't deserve this.

892
00:55:05,400 --> 00:55:07,060
他也不该得到你!
He doesn't deserve you.

893
00:55:08,700 --> 00:55:10,000
我的脖子!
My neck!

894
00:55:14,680 --> 00:55:18,880
他们让我觉得自己是个傻瓜, Jan.
I feel like an idiot.
They made me look like a fool, Jan.

895
00:55:19,550 --> 00:55:22,580
我真想把"深入追击"的...
I was thinking of going down
to that lnside Access place...

896
00:55:23,050 --> 00:55:26,020
...那个Mac McGrath揪出来痛打一顿
...and giving Mac McGrath
the beating of a lifetime.

897
00:55:26,420 --> 00:55:29,720
听起来不错,但你犯不着和他们一样
That sounds like fun,
but don't stoop to their level.

898
00:55:30,230 --> 00:55:32,060
你比那些人好一万倍, Deedsy.
You're better than that, Deedsy.

899
00:55:32,460 --> 00:55:35,990
所以,不要理会他们
我们永远在这里支持你
So hang in there.
And know that we are always here for you.

900
00:55:38,030 --> 00:55:41,400
谢谢你, Jan.
我叔公开的公司确实非常了不起
Thanks, Jan.
My uncle really built an amazing company.

901
00:55:41,970 --> 00:55:45,200
他为5万人提供了工作
Because of him, 50,000 people have jobs.

902
00:55:45,740 --> 00:55:48,230
他还经常做许多好事
And he always tried to do the right thing.

903
00:55:49,310 --> 00:55:51,580
这么说, 他是个很不错的人
Well, he does sound amazing.

904
00:55:52,120 --> 00:55:55,350
别忘了, 你很像他!
But don't forget, he was related to you.

905
00:55:55,790 --> 00:56:00,120
别再说那些了,说说关于那个女孩儿的事
Enough about that. Tell me more about this girl.

906
00:56:01,390 --> 00:56:05,020
她很不错, 和我一样, 来自一个小镇
She's nice, a small-town kid, like me.

907
00:56:05,860 --> 00:56:08,800
Deeds, 你这个变态的混球....
Deedsy, you sick-ass mo' fo'....

908
00:56:08,870 --> 00:56:12,360
你还不抓紧时间,不然她就跟别人跑了
You got to tap that
before she starts boning other guys, kid.

909
00:56:12,970 --> 00:56:13,990
Boo-Yah!
Boo-Yah!

910
00:56:16,070 --> 00:56:19,440
他以为是你写的!
He thinks it's you! He thinks it's you!

911
00:56:21,080 --> 00:56:25,170
- 来吧,Cedar. 打起精神来
- 接球吧
-Let's go, Cedar. Put some steam on it, kid.
-Here it comes.

912
00:56:27,720 --> 00:56:30,480
嘿,你想谋杀我呀,你真有两下子!
He's trying to kill me. You're good at this.

913
00:56:30,550 --> 00:56:33,820
你约我打球,我以为你会打
When you asked me to play,
I thought you'd done this before.

914
00:56:33,890 --> 00:56:36,620
Johnny McEnroe 说这玩意儿很简单
No, Johnny McEnroe said it was wicked easy.

915
00:56:36,860 --> 00:56:39,090
而且我叔公也很喜欢,对吧?
Plus, it was my uncle's favorite game, right?

916
00:56:39,160 --> 00:56:41,790
- 你怎么知道的?
- 从他日记里读到的
-How'd you know that?
-I read it in his diary.

917
00:56:42,730 --> 00:56:43,720
是吗?
Really?

918
00:56:44,730 --> 00:56:46,570
我不知道他还写日记
I didn't know he kept a diary.

919
00:56:50,940 --> 00:56:52,370
抱歉,伙计
Sorry about that, dude.

920
00:56:52,780 --> 00:56:54,830
没关系, 那家伙刚加入
It's okay. He's a new member.

921
00:56:55,650 --> 00:56:56,740
球童!
Ball boy.

922
00:56:57,850 --> 00:56:58,810
球童!
Ball boy!

923
00:57:01,220 --> 00:57:03,210
来吧, 我准备好了
All right, baby, I'm ready for you.

924
00:57:07,860 --> 00:57:09,020
你还好吧?
You okay?

925
00:57:09,260 --> 00:57:12,060
- 小意思 !
- Anderson, 你一定在偷着高兴,是吧?
-Not a problem.
-Anderson, you liked that, didn't you?

926
00:57:12,130 --> 00:57:13,290
是的
I did.

927
00:57:13,500 --> 00:57:15,900
听着, Deeds, 有个好消息
Listen, Deeds, I got some good news.

928
00:57:15,970 --> 00:57:18,160
那些文件明天就可以签字了
Those papers will be ready to sign tomorrow.

929
00:57:18,230 --> 00:57:21,500
